People wrote in about the plant, Angela.
人们写信来问那株植物的事，安吉拉。

546
00:25:16.420 --> 00:25:18.000
It's the first thing I noticed.
这是我注意到的第一件事。

547
00:25:18.180 --> 00:25:19.400
42 seconds.
42秒。

548
00:25:19.780 --> 00:25:22.740
Spotted a potted plant is what I wrote in my notes.
我在笔记里写的是：发现了一盆盆栽。

549
00:25:22.900 --> 00:25:23.860
And it's very cute.
而且它非常可爱。

550
00:25:23.860 --> 00:25:27.240
And it's going to stay on the little desk in Michael Scott Paper Company.
它会一直放在迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司的小桌子上。

551
00:25:27.700 --> 00:25:31.400
Well, for a long time, we've wondered who would bring in the potted plants at reception.
嗯，长期以来，我们一直很好奇是谁把接待处的盆栽搬进来的。

552
00:25:31.580 --> 00:25:32.700
I guess this solves it.
我想这下有答案了。

553
00:25:32.780 --> 00:25:33.300
It was Pam.
是帕姆。

554
00:25:33.440 --> 00:25:34.240
It was Pam.
是帕姆。

555
00:25:34.740 --> 00:25:41.100
While Pam and Jim are walking into the parking lot, Michael has wedged his car between two other cars.
当帕姆和吉姆走进停车场时，迈克尔把他的车硬挤在另外两辆车中间。

556
00:25:41.100 --> 00:25:44.580
And he's trying to shimmy out over the back.
他正试着从后座挪出来。

557
00:25:44.740 --> 00:25:46.520
Holding the Cheetos, by the way.
顺便说一下，手里还拿着奇多。

558
00:25:46.840 --> 00:25:47.100
Yes.
没错。

559
00:25:47.560 --> 00:25:50.360
Jenna, Steve ripped his pants in this scene.
珍娜，史蒂夫在这一幕里把裤子撕破了。

560
00:25:50.480 --> 00:25:51.040
He did?
真的吗？

561
00:25:51.320 --> 00:25:51.560
Yeah.
是的。

562
00:25:52.100 --> 00:25:55.120
He was trying to scooch over the back of the PT Cruiser.
他当时正试着从那辆PT漫步者车的后座挪过去。

563
00:25:55.240 --> 00:25:59.440
And his pants got hung up on the back of the little convertible part.
结果裤子被那个敞篷车顶的后部挂住了。

564
00:25:59.520 --> 00:25:59.800
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

565
00:26:00.160 --> 00:26:01.300
And he's scooching.
他还在那儿挪啊挪。

566
00:26:01.600 --> 00:26:02.900
It's in the bloopers.
花絮里有这一段。

567
00:26:03.160 --> 00:26:04.640
And I was going to play it.
我本来打算放出来的。

568
00:26:04.640 --> 00:26:11.380
But the majority of the bloopers is Steve scooching and grunting, trying to get over the back hump of the car.
但大部分花絮都是史蒂夫在那儿挪动和哼唧，试图翻过车后的隆起部分。

569
00:26:11.520 --> 00:26:15.080
And then he finally says, I'm going to need a new pair of pants.
最后他终于说，我得换条新裤子了。

570
00:26:15.700 --> 00:26:16.100
Oh.
噢。

571
00:26:17.140 --> 00:26:18.540
That just made me laugh.
那段真的把我逗笑了。

572
00:26:18.760 --> 00:26:19.380
You know what?
你知道吗？

573
00:26:19.400 --> 00:26:23.120
I'll put the blooper in our stories because it's really one you have to watch to appreciate.
我会把这段花絮发到我们的快拍里，因为这真的得亲眼看才能体会到其中的乐趣。

574
00:26:23.800 --> 00:26:26.220
Now we go to our opening credits.
现在进入片头字幕。

575
00:26:26.800 --> 00:26:31.780
And they are all new this episode in honor of Michael Scott Paper Company.
为了向迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司致敬，这一集的片头是全新的。

576
00:26:32.080 --> 00:26:33.500
I was very excited for you.
我当时特别为你感到兴奋。

577
00:26:33.500 --> 00:26:37.740
I was like, oh, I bet Jenna has a whole breakdown because you've done a whole thing about the opening credits.
我心想，噢，我敢打赌珍娜肯定会做一个详细的拆解，因为你之前专门做过关于片头字幕的内容。

578
00:26:38.040 --> 00:26:39.760
First of all, I did not remember this.
首先，我完全不记得这回事了。

579
00:26:39.840 --> 00:26:42.020
So when this came on, I was so delighted.
所以当它出现时，我感到非常惊喜。

580
00:26:42.020 --> 00:26:46.980
And then all the memories came flooding back of us filming these new opening credits.
然后，我们拍摄这些新片头时的所有记忆都涌现了出来。

581
00:26:47.560 --> 00:26:49.400
They were also not in the script.
它们也不在剧本里。

582
00:26:49.880 --> 00:26:51.660
This was Mindy Kaling's idea.
这是敏迪·卡灵的主意。

583
00:26:52.500 --> 00:26:55.300
Lee and Gene said they absolutely loved getting to shoot them.
李和吉恩说他们非常喜欢拍摄这些镜头。

584
00:26:55.420 --> 00:26:59.100
And they really tried to match the tone and style of the original main titles.
他们确实努力去匹配原版片头的基调和风格。

585
00:26:59.100 --> 00:27:05.840
So I did a whole breakdown of the Michael Scott Paper Company main titles and our usual main titles.
所以我对迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司的片头和我们平时的片头做了一个完整的对比拆解。

586
00:27:05.860 --> 00:27:09.600
And they match up almost shot for shot.
它们几乎是镜头对镜头地一一对应。

587
00:27:10.060 --> 00:27:11.140
It's pretty cool.
这真的很酷。

588
00:27:11.400 --> 00:27:12.340
That's awesome.
太棒了。

589
00:27:12.560 --> 00:27:16.780
I have some fun tidbits about some of the things we saw in those opening credits.
关于我们在那些片头里看到的一些东西，我有一些有趣的细节要分享。

590
00:27:16.980 --> 00:27:17.120
Okay.
好的。

591
00:27:17.120 --> 00:27:20.380
First of all, the goldfish on Michael's desk.
首先，迈克尔桌上的金鱼。

592
00:27:20.840 --> 00:27:21.440
Oh, yeah.
噢，对。

593
00:27:21.500 --> 00:27:23.780
This all happens about one minute, 18 seconds, right?
这一切发生在大约一分十八秒的时候，对吧？

594
00:27:23.920 --> 00:27:26.180
There's a great overview of the whole room.
有一个关于整个房间的精彩全景镜头。

595
00:27:26.440 --> 00:27:30.140
We got a fan mail flurry about this goldfish lady.
我们收到了很多关于这位金鱼女士的粉丝来信。

596
00:27:30.460 --> 00:27:30.800
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

597
00:27:31.220 --> 00:27:37.780
Remember last week we talked about the Jerry Maguire goldfish and how Michael and Pam had their Jerry Maguire moment.
还记得上周我们谈到《甜心先生》里的金鱼，以及迈克尔和帕姆如何拥有了他们的《甜心先生》时刻吗？

598
00:27:38.500 --> 00:27:42.340
Well, Michael is going to have a goldfish on his desk now.
嗯，现在迈克尔的桌上要放一条金鱼了。

599
00:27:43.500 --> 00:27:52.020
But fan mail flurry points out that there is going to be a different goldfish every time we cut to a shot of Michael's desk.
但粉丝来信指出，每次我们切换到迈克尔桌子的镜头时，金鱼都会换成另一条。

600
00:27:52.480 --> 00:27:54.100
And there is a reason for that.
这背后是有原因的。

601
00:27:54.840 --> 00:27:58.600
Randy Cordray said this was an Easter egg that they planted in these episodes.
兰迪·科德雷说这是他们在这些剧集中埋下的一个彩蛋。

602
00:27:58.860 --> 00:28:00.340
It's never talked about.
从来没人提起过。

603
00:28:00.560 --> 00:28:03.560
But the idea was that Michael could not keep this fish alive.
但原本的设定是迈克尔根本养不活这条鱼。

604
00:28:04.380 --> 00:28:09.500
Randy told me that every Friday they would give the goldfish to a crew member who wanted it.
兰迪告诉我，每周五他们都会把金鱼送给想要的工作人员。

605
00:28:09.840 --> 00:28:13.040
And then they would replace it with a new fish for the next episode.
然后下一集再换一条新的。

606
00:28:13.460 --> 00:28:16.080
So moving forward, folks, I will track the fish.
所以各位，接下来我会追踪这条鱼。

607
00:28:16.240 --> 00:28:19.200
It starts as your standard orange goldfish.
它一开始就是那种普通的橙色金鱼。

608
00:28:19.860 --> 00:28:20.120
Okay.
好的。

609
00:28:21.380 --> 00:28:22.360
Goldfish tracker.
金鱼追踪器。

610
00:28:23.240 --> 00:28:29.380
Next up, I would really like to talk about the stapler that BJ is using in the opening credits.
接下来，我真的很想聊聊片头里BJ用的那个订书机。

611
00:28:29.380 --> 00:28:36.180
It is a paper pro stapler, and we were obsessed with it in Michael Scott Paper Company.
那是Paper Pro牌的订书机，我们在拍“迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司”那几集时对它简直着了迷。

612
00:28:37.240 --> 00:28:37.780
Obsessed.
非常着迷。

613
00:28:38.060 --> 00:28:38.340
Why?
为什么？

614
00:28:38.680 --> 00:28:42.100
It is the greatest stapler you will ever use, ever.
它是你用过最棒的订书机，没有之一。

615
00:28:42.780 --> 00:28:44.000
Phil Shea let me keep one.
菲尔·谢伊让我留了一个。

616
00:28:44.120 --> 00:28:45.220
I still have it.
我现在还留着呢。

617
00:28:45.560 --> 00:28:50.280
You do not have to push on it the way BJ is in the opening credits.
你根本不需要像片头里BJ那样用力按它。

618
00:28:50.280 --> 00:28:52.400
He is operating the stapler incorrectly.
他使用订书机的方法不对。

619
00:28:52.400 --> 00:29:01.660
You just give it a little squeeze, and the air pressure, some sort of mechanism, makes it staple perfectly.
你只需要轻轻一压，靠气压或者某种机械装置，它就能完美地订好。

620
00:29:02.100 --> 00:29:03.320
I looked it up.
我查过了。

621
00:29:03.820 --> 00:29:05.620
Here's how it is described.
它是这样描述的。

622
00:29:05.940 --> 00:29:06.480
Okay.
好的。

623
00:29:07.180 --> 00:29:13.580
The paper pro is the first engineering breakthrough in staplers since, well, the stapler.
Paper Pro是订书机自发明以来，在工程学上的首次重大突破。

624
00:29:14.240 --> 00:29:24.600
Push it with one finger's worth of effort, and a spring-loaded mechanism drives the staple with 30 pounds of force through up to 20 sheets of paper.
只需用一根手指的力气按下去，弹簧驱动装置就能产生30磅的压力，一次订透多达20张纸。

625
00:29:25.080 --> 00:29:25.720
Wow.
哇。

626
00:29:26.100 --> 00:29:27.480
We loved that stapler.
我们当时超爱那个订书机。

627
00:29:27.700 --> 00:29:28.500
We loved it.
真的很爱。

628
00:29:28.780 --> 00:29:36.200
Of all the things I thought we would talk about today, I did not think we'd talk about a super air pressure-powered stapler.
在今天所有我想聊的话题里，我真没想到我们会讨论一个超级气压驱动的订书机。

629
00:29:36.520 --> 00:29:37.720
I recommend it.
我推荐大家试试。

630
00:29:37.980 --> 00:29:39.920
I'm dying to use one.
我迫不及待想用一次了。

631
00:29:40.680 --> 00:29:49.260
Finally, the copier that you see in the opening credits and throughout this episode is the broken copier from the surplus.
最后，片头和本集中出现的复印机，就是“剩余物资”那一集里那台坏掉的复印机。

632
00:29:49.560 --> 00:29:51.620
I love that written on the side, it says trash.
我喜欢它侧面写着“垃圾”二字。

633
00:29:51.960 --> 00:29:52.320
I know.
我知道。

634
00:29:53.020 --> 00:29:55.200
That copier is just haunting Pam.
那台复印机简直是帕姆的噩梦。

635
00:29:55.340 --> 00:29:59.560
She's lost her comfortable chair, and now she's back with this horrible copier.
她失去了舒服的椅子，现在又回到了这台破烂复印机身边。

636
00:29:59.680 --> 00:30:01.000
What has she done to her life?
她的人生到底经历了什么？

637
00:30:01.120 --> 00:30:03.520
You know that was sitting out by the dumpsters.
你知道那台机器当时就放在垃圾箱旁边。

638
00:30:03.740 --> 00:30:06.240
They wrote trash on it and set it out.
他们写上“垃圾”然后把它扔在那儿。

639
00:30:07.200 --> 00:30:07.760
Ah.
啊。

640
00:30:08.520 --> 00:30:14.940
So right at the beginning of their first day of the Michael Scott Paper Company, there would have been a series of talking heads.
所以就在迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司开业第一天的开头，本来应该有一系列采访镜头。

641
00:30:15.680 --> 00:30:16.840
Ryan had one.
瑞安有一个。

642
00:30:17.040 --> 00:30:18.160
Michael had one.
迈克尔有一个。

643
00:30:18.680 --> 00:30:19.740
Pam had one.
帕姆有一个。

644
00:30:19.900 --> 00:30:21.400
About her first day.
关于她的第一天。

645
00:30:21.920 --> 00:30:25.120
And I thought it was really sweet and also made me a little curious.
我觉得那段真的很温馨，也让我有点好奇。

646
00:30:25.140 --> 00:30:26.180
I think we need to hear it.
我觉得我们得听听看。

647
00:30:27.000 --> 00:30:28.220
Embarking on a new adventure.
开启一段新的冒险。

648
00:30:28.980 --> 00:30:31.960
There was a fork in the road, and I took the road less traveled.
人生路口，我选择了那条人迹罕至的路。

649
00:30:32.900 --> 00:30:33.780
Never traveled.
从未有人走过。

650
00:30:34.240 --> 00:30:35.380
Not even a road, really.
甚至算不上是一条路。

651
00:30:35.640 --> 00:30:36.460
More of a path.
更像是一条小路。

652
00:30:36.760 --> 00:30:39.340
With a sign that says, those who pass shall die.
上面还有个牌子，写着“擅入者死”。

653
00:30:39.560 --> 00:30:40.840
And a skull and crossbones.
还有一个骷髅交叉骨的标志。

654
00:30:41.880 --> 00:30:44.640
The other road was kind of like Putnam Road.
另一条路有点像普特南路。

655
00:30:46.280 --> 00:30:48.000
That's a really boring road in Scranton.
那是斯克兰顿一条非常无聊的路。

656
00:30:48.000 --> 00:30:52.550
So these were the two paths that you were choosing between.
所以这就是你当时面临的两条路。

657
00:30:53.210 --> 00:30:57.550
But guys, in Scranton, I Google image Putnam Road.
但是伙计们，在斯克兰顿，我谷歌了一下普特南路的图片。

658
00:30:57.750 --> 00:30:59.530
It looks like a fine road.
看起来还不错。

659
00:30:59.750 --> 00:31:00.690
Here's something crazy.
有件疯狂的事。

660
00:31:00.770 --> 00:31:06.430
I worked at Putnam Investments as an executive secretary for years.
我曾在普特南投资公司做过多年的行政秘书。

661
00:31:06.650 --> 00:31:13.530
That was my last full-time job I had as an executive assistant before I was able to earn my living full-time as an actor.
那是我在全职做演员谋生之前，最后一份全职行政助理的工作。

662
00:31:13.530 --> 00:31:14.290
Woo!
呜！

663
00:31:14.850 --> 00:31:17.330
Yeah, that's a full-circle life moment.
没错，这真是人生圆满的一刻。

664
00:31:17.670 --> 00:31:21.470
Well, back upstairs, you know, this is such a funny scene.
回到楼上，你知道，这一幕太搞笑了。

665
00:31:22.350 --> 00:31:27.670
Kelly is sort of leaning up on Jim's desk, and she's just sort of mumbling things.
凯莉靠在吉姆的桌子上，嘴里嘟囔着什么。

666
00:31:27.870 --> 00:31:29.590
Like, Jim's like, you're where you're not really talking to me.
吉姆就像是说，你根本没在跟我说话。

667
00:31:29.730 --> 00:31:33.150
She is just waiting for Charles to say Kelly.
她只是在等查尔斯叫“凯莉”。

668
00:31:34.170 --> 00:31:37.370
And then she runs in, and she's like, you wanted me?
然后她跑进去说，你找我吗？

669
00:31:37.790 --> 00:31:39.610
And he's like, no, no, no, I meant that Kelly.
而他却说，不，不，不，我指的是那个凯莉。

670
00:31:39.770 --> 00:31:42.150
And this is when we meet Aaron.
这时我们见到了亚伦。

671
00:31:42.570 --> 00:31:43.010
Yes.
是的。

672
00:31:43.010 --> 00:31:51.090
Jim has this fantastic talking head that he says that Kelly thinks if she says you wanted me enough, that Charles will, in fact, want her.
吉姆有个很棒的采访镜头，他说凯莉以为只要她多说几次“你找我吗”，查尔斯就真的会找她。

673
00:31:51.330 --> 00:31:53.070
It's not the worst plan she's ever had.
这还不是她想出的最烂的计划。

674
00:31:54.350 --> 00:31:55.550
Lady, this made me think.
女士，这让我陷入了沉思。

675
00:31:56.070 --> 00:31:58.010
Like, this is like self-fulfilling prophecy.
这就像是自我实现的预言。

676
00:31:59.030 --> 00:32:01.550
Like, Kelly is using self-fulfilling prophecy.
凯莉是在利用自我实现的预言。

677
00:32:01.910 --> 00:32:11.170
My mom used to have this saying, and I think it's like paraphrasing Scripture and Proverbs, but speak of what is not as if it were so, and it shall become.
我妈妈以前常说一句话，我想那是对《圣经》和《箴言》的意译，即“以无为有，终将成真”。

678
00:32:11.490 --> 00:32:12.070
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

679
00:32:12.070 --> 00:32:18.270
And I think I was, like, sort of in a very deep place when I was watching this episode.
我觉得我在看这一集的时候，思绪非常深沉。

680
00:32:18.590 --> 00:32:25.850
I had some things in my life that I had sort of written out, like something I was meditating about, praying about, and it was coming to fruition.
我生活中有些事情是我写下来的，是我一直在冥想、祈祷的事情，而且它们正在实现。

681
00:32:25.850 --> 00:32:33.450
And I was trying to plant these seeds of, like, positive good intention, right, to then have this great harvest of this good thing.
我当时正试图播下这些积极、善意的种子，对吧，为了最终能收获这些美好的果实。

682
00:32:33.450 --> 00:32:42.610
And when you watch The Office through that filter, you're like, Kelly, Kelly is practicing self-fulfilling prophecy.
当你透过这个滤镜看《办公室》时，你会觉得，凯莉，凯莉是在实践自我实现的预言。

683
00:32:42.610 --> 00:32:43.890
It's great.
太棒了。

684
00:32:44.010 --> 00:32:45.790
I use that all the time.
我一直都在用这一招。

685
00:32:45.950 --> 00:32:47.270
We talk about that.
我们谈论过这个。

686
00:32:47.430 --> 00:32:47.590
Yeah.
是的。

687
00:32:47.810 --> 00:32:53.610
I mean, just in the formation of this podcast, we must have said what we wanted for two years.
我是说，单就这个播客的筹备来说，我们肯定说了两年我们想要什么。

688
00:32:53.810 --> 00:32:54.050
Yeah.
是的。

689
00:32:54.050 --> 00:32:58.090
Before we developed this show and signed a contract.
在我们开发这个节目并签合同之前。

690
00:32:58.450 --> 00:32:59.530
Speak the positive.
说出积极的话。

691
00:32:59.970 --> 00:33:00.790
Speak it.
说出来。

692
00:33:00.970 --> 00:33:07.630
I always say when you blow out your birthday candles, you should tell everyone your wish because the more people who know,
我总是说，当你吹灭生日蜡烛时，你应该告诉大家你的愿望，因为知道的人越多，

693
00:33:07.850 --> 00:33:10.790
there's more people invested in helping you make it come true.
就有更多的人投入进来帮助你实现它。

694
00:33:11.010 --> 00:33:11.230
Yeah.
是的。

695
00:33:11.430 --> 00:33:12.310
Share your wishes.
分享你的愿望。

696
00:33:12.650 --> 00:33:13.150
Share it.
分享出来。

697
00:33:13.150 --> 00:33:14.350
I love that.
我喜欢这个。

698
00:33:14.510 --> 00:33:15.630
I had to share that.
我必须分享一下。

699
00:33:16.150 --> 00:33:20.530
Well, I have got a bit of a bombshell regarding this scene.
好吧，关于这一幕，我有个重磅消息要宣布。

700
00:33:21.010 --> 00:33:21.490
What?
什么？

701
00:33:21.730 --> 00:33:22.730
A full bombshell.
简直是个重磅炸弹。

702
00:33:23.070 --> 00:33:23.290
What?
什么？

703
00:33:23.650 --> 00:33:26.370
So, you know, Charles says, I wasn't talking about you, Kelly.
所以，你知道，查尔斯说，我不是在说你，凯莉。

704
00:33:26.490 --> 00:33:27.750
I was talking about the other Kelly.
我是在说另一个凯莉。

705
00:33:27.930 --> 00:33:33.310
And they eventually settle on the fact that they will call the second Kelly by her middle name, Erin.
他们最终决定，以后就叫第二个凯莉中间名，艾琳。

706
00:33:33.770 --> 00:33:34.130
Yeah.
是啊。

707
00:33:34.510 --> 00:33:37.330
The original name for Ellie's character.
艾莉这个角色的最初名字。

708
00:33:37.710 --> 00:33:38.190
What?
什么？

709
00:33:38.190 --> 00:33:41.010
The one that appears in the table draft.
出现在剧本初稿里的那个名字。

710
00:33:41.230 --> 00:33:41.450
What?
什么？

711
00:33:41.810 --> 00:33:42.910
Was not Kelly.
不是凯莉。

712
00:33:43.150 --> 00:33:44.790
It was not Erin.
也不是艾琳。

713
00:33:45.710 --> 00:33:47.190
Her name was Mary.
她的名字叫玛丽。

714
00:33:47.930 --> 00:33:48.530
Mary!
玛丽！

715
00:33:48.950 --> 00:33:49.450
Yeah.
没错。

716
00:33:49.690 --> 00:33:52.830
And this scene was not a thing where they have the same name.
而且这场戏原本也不是关于她们同名的。

717
00:33:52.970 --> 00:33:54.070
That was a late addition.
那是后来才加进去的。

718
00:33:54.590 --> 00:33:55.570
Oh, wow.
噢，哇。

719
00:33:55.570 --> 00:33:57.210
I love this scene.
我喜欢这场戏。

720
00:33:57.330 --> 00:33:57.730
I know.
我知道。

721
00:33:57.810 --> 00:33:58.210
Me too.
我也是。

722
00:33:59.070 --> 00:34:01.950
Well, fan question from Kelly Ann M.
好，来自凯莉·安·M的粉丝提问。

723
00:34:02.310 --> 00:34:06.410
who says, we need to track Erin's hair progression.
她说，我们需要追踪艾琳的发色变化过程。

724
00:34:06.850 --> 00:34:08.490
When did she go red?
她是什么时候染成红发的？

725
00:34:09.090 --> 00:34:13.890
She will eventually win cutest redhead in the office, but she's a brunette here.
她最终会成为办公室里最可爱的红发女郎，但现在她是深棕色头发。

726
00:34:14.070 --> 00:34:15.150
We need to track it.
我们需要追踪一下。

727
00:34:16.070 --> 00:34:18.350
Well, Lee Eisenberg filled me in on this.
嗯，李·艾森伯格告诉了我这件事。

728
00:34:18.550 --> 00:34:20.170
Well, I remember some of this.
嗯，我记得一些。

729
00:34:20.550 --> 00:34:27.590
He said when Ellie showed up for her very first day of work, her hair color was almost identical to mine.
他说当艾莉第一天来上班时，她的发色和我的几乎一模一样。

730
00:34:27.590 --> 00:34:27.910
Yep.
没错。

731
00:34:28.410 --> 00:34:30.430
And everyone freaked out.
大家都吓坏了。

732
00:34:30.710 --> 00:34:31.110
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

733
00:34:31.250 --> 00:34:40.250
They were not trying to tell a story that Pam was being replaced by a sort of lookalike person.
他们并不是想讲一个帕姆被长相相似的人取代的故事。

734
00:34:40.250 --> 00:34:48.750
And they were really worried that if they put her on camera, having the same color hair, that it was going to tell a story they weren't telling.
他们真的很担心如果让她出镜，发色又一样，会传达出他们不想表达的意思。

735
00:34:49.190 --> 00:34:49.290
Yeah.
是啊。

736
00:34:50.050 --> 00:34:56.230
So they had to change the whole schedule for the day and color her hair.
所以他们不得不改变当天的整个拍摄计划，去给她的头发染色。

737
00:34:56.230 --> 00:35:00.990
I was in the hair and makeup trailer when she was getting her hair colored by Kim Ferry.
当时我在化妆车里，金·费里正在给她染发。

738
00:35:01.310 --> 00:35:04.630
And I guess Kim just has a drawer of hair color.
我猜金那里刚好有一抽屉的染发剂。

739
00:35:04.870 --> 00:35:05.350
Sure.
当然。

740
00:35:05.650 --> 00:35:09.870
And they came up with this sort of brunette color, which will now evolve.
他们想出了这种深棕色，以后还会再变。

741
00:35:10.230 --> 00:35:16.010
The character of Erin was also not originally meant to become a full-time regular character.
艾琳这个角色最初也没打算成为全职常驻角色。

742
00:35:16.010 --> 00:35:18.370
This was just going to be a few episodes.
原本只打算让她演几集。

743
00:35:18.770 --> 00:35:20.670
So we will track it.
所以我们会追踪这个过程。

744
00:35:20.790 --> 00:35:28.870
But I believe her hair is going to get to sort of change over to that red color as they make her a more permanent character on the show.
但我相信随着她成为剧中的常驻角色，她的发色会逐渐变成那种红色。

745
00:35:29.290 --> 00:35:29.790
Yeah.
是啊。

746
00:35:29.970 --> 00:35:31.130
I remember that day.
我记得那天。

747
00:35:31.310 --> 00:35:33.610
And Ellie is such a team player, you know.
艾莉真是个很有团队精神的人，你知道的。

748
00:35:33.910 --> 00:35:35.510
And my memory's correct.
如果我的记忆没错的话。

749
00:35:35.510 --> 00:35:38.030
They died at one time and then died it again.
她们当时染了一次，后来又染了一次。

750
00:35:38.310 --> 00:35:38.870
Oh, boy.
天哪。

751
00:35:39.110 --> 00:35:39.370
Yeah.
是啊。

752
00:35:39.830 --> 00:35:40.510
Oh, boy.
天哪。

753
00:35:41.390 --> 00:35:45.090
Michael Scott Paper Company has kind of come already to a standstill.
迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司现在陷入了僵局。

754
00:35:45.630 --> 00:35:46.750
They don't know what to do.
他们不知道该怎么办。

755
00:35:46.930 --> 00:35:47.750
They're like, what do we do now?
他们就像在说，现在我们该做什么？

756
00:35:47.930 --> 00:35:49.710
They're just sitting there looking at each other.
他们只是坐在那儿面面相觑。

757
00:35:50.250 --> 00:35:50.430
Yeah.
没错。

758
00:35:50.570 --> 00:35:54.230
Michael's working on his evite for his pancake luncheon.
迈克尔正在为他的煎饼午宴写电子邀请函。

759
00:35:54.430 --> 00:36:02.870
We had a fan catch from Ria V and Abby M who noticed if you look closely, it says that the luncheon is going to take place on Saturday.
有位粉丝Ria V和Abby M提醒我们，如果仔细看，会发现午宴定在周六举行。

760
00:36:03.210 --> 00:36:04.350
I saw that, too.
我也注意到了。

761
00:36:05.010 --> 00:36:10.630
Also, during this scene, you can hear the sounds of toilets flushing through the pipes overhead.
另外，在这场戏里，你能听到头顶管道传来冲厕所的声音。

762
00:36:10.850 --> 00:36:12.950
You're really getting a sense of this workspace.
你真的能感受到这个办公空间的情况。

763
00:36:12.950 --> 00:36:20.890
Anyways, so we could actually hear toilets flushing if somebody used the real bathrooms outside.
总之，如果外面有人用真正的洗手间，我们确实能听到冲水声。

764
00:36:22.810 --> 00:36:25.850
So while we were shooting, they would not allow anyone in there.
所以拍摄的时候，他们不准任何人进去。

765
00:36:25.950 --> 00:36:30.570
But while we rehearsed or while we were waiting to shoot, people could use the bathrooMs.
但在排练或等待拍摄时，人们可以使用洗手间。

766
00:36:30.570 --> 00:36:34.370
And so we would really sit in that room and hear flushing toilets.
所以我们确实会坐在那个房间里听着冲水声。

767
00:36:36.690 --> 00:36:41.590
And I also don't know if you noticed the spots that BJ and I are sitting in.
我不知道你们有没有注意到我和BJ坐的位置。

768
00:36:41.750 --> 00:36:51.230
When we first walked into that room, our natural inclination was to sit across from one another at the table because it gave you maximum space for your elbows.
当我们第一次走进那个房间时，我们的本能反应是坐在桌子对面，因为那样胳膊肘的空间最大。

769
00:36:51.710 --> 00:36:51.890
Sure, sure.
确实，确实。

770
00:36:51.890 --> 00:36:55.190
You know, but you couldn't shoot us that way.
你知道，但那样拍不到我们。

771
00:36:55.390 --> 00:37:07.190
We had to both sort of sit with our backs like scrunched up against that wall kind of next to each other facing Michael because it was literally the only way to get us on camera.
我们俩不得不背靠着墙，挤在一起面对迈克尔，因为这真的是唯一能把我们拍进镜头的方法。

772
00:37:07.630 --> 00:37:17.650
Last week in Dream Team for the DVD commentary for that episode, Matt Sohn actually talked about this episode and how hard it was to shoot in that room because of the angles.
上周在《梦之队》那一集的DVD评论音轨里，马特·索恩确实谈到了这一集，以及因为角度问题在那个房间拍摄有多难。

773
00:37:17.650 --> 00:37:19.070
Exactly what you were talking about.
和你刚才说的一模一样。

774
00:37:19.210 --> 00:37:20.690
They kept catching each other.
他们总是会拍到对方。

775
00:37:20.950 --> 00:37:23.670
Our two camera operators kept catching each other in the shot.
我们的两名摄影师总是会把对方拍进镜头里。

776
00:37:24.110 --> 00:37:28.150
So they had to sort of position you guys so that they could get these single camera shots of you.
所以他们不得不调整你们的位置，以便能拍到你们的单人镜头。

777
00:37:28.430 --> 00:37:33.270
Yeah, I think that's something you don't think about when you watch the scene is how there's all these extra people in the room.
是啊，我觉得看戏的时候你不会想到房间里还有那么多额外的人。

778
00:37:33.410 --> 00:37:33.670
Yeah.
没错。

779
00:37:33.970 --> 00:37:36.670
But they're magically avoiding one another on camera.
但他们在镜头里神奇地避开了彼此。

780
00:37:36.930 --> 00:37:43.490
But at the same time, Steve as Michael can't walk from his desk to the poker table without bonking his leg into things.
但与此同时，饰演迈克尔的史蒂夫从办公桌走到扑克桌时，腿总会撞到东西。

781
00:37:43.590 --> 00:37:44.770
You know, it's like that tight.
你知道，就是那么挤。

782
00:37:44.770 --> 00:37:45.124
Right.
对。

783
00:37:45.124 --> 00:37:51.090
Well, now Michael is going to ask Pam to make 800 copies of his unparalleled customer service coupon.
好了，现在迈克尔要让帕姆复印800份他的“无与伦比的客户服务”优惠券。

784
00:37:51.330 --> 00:37:54.250
But Pam has a talking head, and I really relate to this.
但帕姆有个采访镜头，我对此深有感触。

785
00:37:54.770 --> 00:38:01.510
She says, if I make this one copy, then I'll become the girl who makes copies, and then I'm basically a receptionist again.
她说，如果我复印了这一份，我就成了那个负责复印的女孩，那我基本上又变回前台了。

786
00:38:01.990 --> 00:38:07.170
And I don't know if you noticed where the phone was on that table, but it is right in front of Pam.
我不知道你们有没有注意到桌上的电话放在哪儿，它就在帕姆的正前方。

787
00:38:07.490 --> 00:38:10.630
So she's already clearly closest to the phone.
所以很明显，她离电话最近。

788
00:38:10.630 --> 00:38:14.270
And even later, when it rings, Michael says, answer it.
甚至后来电话响的时候，迈克尔还说，去接电话。

789
00:38:14.770 --> 00:38:15.370
I know.
我知道。

790
00:38:15.530 --> 00:38:15.610
Right?
对吧？

791
00:38:15.870 --> 00:38:16.090
Yeah.
是啊。

792
00:38:16.590 --> 00:38:22.910
She's really trying to break out of this role of receptionist, and she refuses to make the copy.
她真的在努力摆脱前台这个角色，所以她拒绝复印。

793
00:38:23.130 --> 00:38:25.230
She doesn't want to go down Putnam Road, guys.
她不想走那条老路，伙计们。

794
00:38:25.450 --> 00:38:26.050
She doesn't.
她不想。

795
00:38:26.170 --> 00:38:28.530
She wants the other path, the more exciting path.
她想要另一条路，那条更令人兴奋的路。

796
00:38:29.010 --> 00:38:32.210
Well, it's a pretty big day for a few other characters at Dunder Mifflin.
好吧，对于邓德·米夫林的其他几位角色来说，今天是个大日子。

797
00:38:32.670 --> 00:38:35.350
Dwight is going to take Andy hunting.
德怀特要带安迪去打猎。

798
00:38:36.390 --> 00:38:37.950
They're like buddy-buddy.
他们好得像哥们儿一样。

799
00:38:37.950 --> 00:38:43.770
There is so much more of this scene where they're sort of wrestling and like doing all this stuff.
这场戏里还有很多他们摔跤之类的互动。

800
00:38:44.150 --> 00:38:45.690
It goes on for so long.
持续了很长时间。

801
00:38:45.850 --> 00:38:46.630
I have no doubt.
我对此深信不疑。

802
00:38:46.830 --> 00:38:55.210
Do not ask the fellas to roughhouse or wrestle in a scene unless you want to have an hour of additional footage of it.
除非你想多拍一个小时的素材，否则千万别让那帮家伙在戏里打闹或摔跤。

803
00:38:55.330 --> 00:39:04.710
Because anytime they had Rainn Wilson and John Krasinski have to do something like that, like last week's knock-knock joke thing, any scuffle.
因为每次雷恩·威尔森和约翰·卡拉辛斯基要演这类戏份时，比如上周那个敲门笑话，或者任何推搡戏。

804
00:39:04.710 --> 00:39:13.950
It's worth a watch in the deleted scenes because those two fellas, they go for so long in all their fake different ways of attacking each other.
删减片段里很值得一看，因为那两个家伙，他们会用各种假装攻击对方的方式纠缠好久。

805
00:39:14.030 --> 00:39:16.910
And they get so into John's personal space.
而且他们靠约翰的私人空间靠得太近了。

806
00:39:17.490 --> 00:39:19.290
And his face is hilarious.
他的表情简直太搞笑了。

807
00:39:19.510 --> 00:39:20.890
I don't know how he kept a straight face.
我不知道他是怎么忍住不笑场的。

808
00:39:21.770 --> 00:39:25.810
Andy had a talking head that was deleted where he talks about this bromance.
安迪原本有一段被删掉的采访，他在里面谈到了这段兄弟情。

809
00:39:25.930 --> 00:39:27.650
You know, we see Dwight's in the episode.
你知道，我们在剧里看到了德怀特的采访。

810
00:39:27.650 --> 00:39:30.990
But Andy had a counterpart one, and I think we need to hear it.
但安迪也有一个对应的采访，我觉得我们应该听听。

811
00:39:31.150 --> 00:39:31.370
Oh.
噢。

812
00:39:32.410 --> 00:39:33.310
Let me tell you something.
让我告诉你一件事。

813
00:39:33.550 --> 00:39:38.250
When Angela and I split, I went through it big time.
当安吉拉和我分手时，我真的非常难熬。

814
00:39:38.670 --> 00:39:39.870
Lost my high notes.
我的高音都唱不出来了。

815
00:39:40.450 --> 00:39:42.510
Top of my range was like, boo.
我音域的最高点就像是，呜。

816
00:39:44.960 --> 00:39:46.020
Then I took some time.
后来我花了一些时间。

817
00:39:46.440 --> 00:39:47.740
I got my heel on.
我振作了起来。

818
00:39:48.040 --> 00:39:49.680
I got some perspective on.
我换了个角度看问题。

819
00:39:50.420 --> 00:39:54.920
And I found a new friend in the most unlikely of places.
然后在最意想不到的地方找到了一个新朋友。

820
00:39:55.780 --> 00:39:56.920
The enemy bin.
敌人的阵营里。

821
00:39:58.980 --> 00:40:00.060
And now...
而现在……

822
00:40:00.060 --> 00:40:00.820
Oh.
噢。

823
00:40:11.930 --> 00:40:13.150
He got his high notes back.
他找回了他的高音。

824
00:40:13.250 --> 00:40:13.770
He did.
确实如此。

825
00:40:14.030 --> 00:40:15.070
He got his heel on.
他振作了起来。

826
00:40:15.150 --> 00:40:16.550
He got his perspective on.
他换了个角度看问题。

827
00:40:16.650 --> 00:40:18.230
And he found it all in the enemy bin.
而且这一切都是在敌人的阵营里找到的。

828
00:40:18.370 --> 00:40:18.830
I know.
我知道。

829
00:40:19.690 --> 00:40:24.130
I also really love the storyline of Charles asking Jim for the rundown.
我也非常喜欢查尔斯让吉姆交出工作总结的那条故事线。

830
00:40:24.350 --> 00:40:24.870
Yes.
没错。

831
00:40:25.290 --> 00:40:28.490
And Jim has no idea what a rundown is.
而吉姆根本不知道什么是工作总结。

832
00:40:28.490 --> 00:40:30.710
And he's not going to ask.
而且他也不打算问。

833
00:40:31.270 --> 00:40:32.370
He's too afraid.
他太害怕了。

834
00:40:32.690 --> 00:40:33.110
I know.
我知道。

835
00:40:33.430 --> 00:40:38.570
So when we reached out to Gene and Lee, they said that this whole rundown story was a late
所以当我们联系吉恩和李时，他们说整个工作总结的故事线是后来

836
00:40:38.570 --> 00:40:38.970
addition.
加进去的。

837
00:40:39.490 --> 00:40:41.350
It was part of a rewrite session.
那是重写会议的一部分。

838
00:40:41.350 --> 00:40:44.390
And you know, we've talked about how some of the writers would break off into these little
你知道，我们之前聊过编剧们有时会分成几个小

839
00:40:44.390 --> 00:40:44.810
pods.
组。

840
00:40:45.450 --> 00:40:50.410
So Paul Lieberstein, Jen Salata, and BJ Novak broke away from the group.
所以保罗·李伯斯汀、简·萨拉塔和B·J·诺瓦克从大组里分了出来。

841
00:40:50.570 --> 00:40:54.570
And in about two hours, they came up with this whole rundown storyline.
在大约两个小时内，他们就想出了整个工作总结的故事线。

842
00:40:54.850 --> 00:40:55.850
I love it.
我喜欢这个。

843
00:40:56.010 --> 00:40:56.730
I know.
我知道。

844
00:40:56.730 --> 00:41:00.550
And then Justin Spitzer said, they thought this was great.
然后贾斯汀·斯皮策说，他们觉得这太棒了。

845
00:41:00.670 --> 00:41:02.630
This sort of rundown was sort of this vague term.
这种所谓的工作总结是一个很模糊的词。

846
00:41:02.630 --> 00:41:05.210
And no one in the writer's room really knew what it meant.
编剧室里没人真正知道它是什么意思。

847
00:41:05.330 --> 00:41:06.290
So they thought, well, that's perfect.
所以他们想，嗯，这太完美了。

848
00:41:06.410 --> 00:41:07.590
Maybe Jim wouldn't know either.
也许吉姆也不会知道。

849
00:41:07.930 --> 00:41:12.750
And they said after the episode aired that they got mail that people were like, yeah,
他们说剧集播出后，他们收到了邮件，人们都在说，是啊，

850
00:41:12.870 --> 00:41:13.670
duh, a rundown.
废话，当然是工作总结。

851
00:41:13.870 --> 00:41:14.670
Yeah, rundown.
没错，工作总结。

852
00:41:14.790 --> 00:41:16.170
Like people had heard of it.
就好像大家以前都听说过一样。

853
00:41:16.270 --> 00:41:17.470
And they were like, no way.
他们当时反应是，绝不可能。

854
00:41:17.710 --> 00:41:19.250
So I looked it up.
所以我查了一下。

855
00:41:19.430 --> 00:41:21.730
I Googled because we're ladies that Google.
我用谷歌搜了，因为我们是会用谷歌的女士。

856
00:41:21.850 --> 00:41:22.230
We are.
我们确实是。

857
00:41:22.230 --> 00:41:24.510
I just wrote, what is a rundown?
我直接写了，什么是工作总结？

858
00:41:24.990 --> 00:41:27.210
And this is what the internet had to say.
这就是网上给出的解释。

859
00:41:28.070 --> 00:41:31.730
In businesses, a rundown is a status report or summary.
在商业中，工作总结就是一份状态报告或摘要。

860
00:41:32.450 --> 00:41:32.790
Yeah.
没错。

861
00:41:33.050 --> 00:41:36.410
I mean, common sense would lead me in that direction.
我的意思是，常识也会引导我往那个方向想。

862
00:41:36.410 --> 00:41:42.370
If I had to guess, I would think, oh, I should make a list of all my current clients and their
如果非要我猜，我会想，哦，我应该列一份我所有现有客户的名单，以及他们的

863
00:41:42.370 --> 00:41:42.770
status.
状态。

864
00:41:42.770 --> 00:41:45.390
Yeah, I think I could have been a little confused.
是啊，我觉得我当时可能会有点困惑。

865
00:41:45.570 --> 00:41:46.930
Like, is a rundown my sales?
比如，工作总结是指我的销售额吗？

866
00:41:47.550 --> 00:41:51.810
Is it like an itemized thing of how much product I move?
是那种详细列出我卖了多少产品的清单吗？

867
00:41:51.970 --> 00:41:56.270
Or is it more just my clients' names and how long they've been my clients?
还是说仅仅是我的客户名单，以及他们成为我客户的时间？

868
00:41:56.490 --> 00:42:00.070
You know, I think there is a little bit of vagueness, like Justin said.
你知道，我觉得确实有点模糊，就像贾斯汀说的那样。

869
00:42:00.410 --> 00:42:04.730
But Jim just needs to ask, what do you want a rundown of?
但吉姆只需要问一句，你想要什么样的工作总结？

870
00:42:04.790 --> 00:42:05.470
My clients?
我的客户？

871
00:42:05.670 --> 00:42:06.650
The inventory?
库存？

872
00:42:06.950 --> 00:42:07.590
What exactly?
到底是什么？

873
00:42:07.990 --> 00:42:08.250
Sales?
销售额？

874
00:42:08.730 --> 00:42:09.810
Well, I'll tell you what.
好吧，我跟你说。

875
00:42:09.810 --> 00:42:16.170
We got a lot of mail on this, and Hannah Q had a strong opinion saying, forgive me for
我们收到了很多关于此事的邮件，汉娜·Q 有个强烈的观点，她说，请原谅我

876
00:42:16.170 --> 00:42:19.470
saying this, but I think I'm on Charles' side when it comes to the rundown.
这么说，但在工作总结这件事上，我觉得我站在查尔斯那边。

877
00:42:19.630 --> 00:42:24.630
I've never had an office job, and even I have a pretty clear idea of what it could or should
我从来没做过办公室工作，即便如此，我也对它可能或应该是什么样

878
00:42:24.630 --> 00:42:25.170
look like.
有个相当清晰的概念。

879
00:42:25.410 --> 00:42:26.290
Come on, Jim.
拜托，吉姆。

880
00:42:26.510 --> 00:42:27.610
You're a smart guy.
你是个聪明人。

881
00:42:27.870 --> 00:42:30.090
Look within and find the rundown.
向内审视，找出那个工作总结。

882
00:42:30.590 --> 00:42:31.810
Hannah's not having it.
汉娜可不买账。

883
00:42:31.950 --> 00:42:32.910
She's not having it.
她完全不买账。

884
00:42:33.410 --> 00:42:39.790
Meanwhile, in the kitchen, we're going to kick off this storyline where Dwight and Andy
与此同时，在厨房里，我们要开启一段剧情，德怀特和安迪

885
00:42:40.410 --> 00:42:42.450
are both kind of flirting with Aaron.
都在跟亚伦调情。

886
00:42:43.330 --> 00:42:47.890
Dwight does this weird thing where he teases her about the office being haunted, and then
德怀特做了一件奇怪的事，他逗她说办公室闹鬼，然后

887
00:42:47.890 --> 00:42:51.390
Andy comes in, and they end up doing a little dance together.
安迪进来了，他们最后还一起跳了段舞。

888
00:42:51.750 --> 00:42:53.630
It's going to get awkward real faSt.
这很快就会变得尴尬起来。

889
00:42:53.770 --> 00:42:54.450
It really is.
确实会。

890
00:42:54.530 --> 00:42:55.910
What happened to their bromance?
他们的兄弟情谊怎么了？

891
00:42:56.390 --> 00:42:57.890
It's already being tested.
已经开始经受考验了。

892
00:42:58.070 --> 00:42:58.490
I know.
我知道。

893
00:42:59.330 --> 00:43:03.210
Jenna, you know, like when you make a personal call, and you know you need to make a personal
珍娜，你知道，就像当你打私人电话时，你知道你需要打这个

894
00:43:03.210 --> 00:43:05.830
call, but, you know, other people can overhear you.
私人电话，但是，你知道，别人能听到。

895
00:43:05.990 --> 00:43:09.070
So you try to practice some form of etiquette in that phone call.
所以你在打电话时会尽量讲究一点礼仪。

896
00:43:09.230 --> 00:43:10.850
Or speak in code a little bit.
或者稍微用点暗语。

897
00:43:10.990 --> 00:43:11.310
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

898
00:43:11.590 --> 00:43:11.850
Yeah.
没错。

899
00:43:12.370 --> 00:43:14.830
That's going to be happening at the Michael Scott Paper Company.
这就要在迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司上演了。

900
00:43:15.110 --> 00:43:16.110
It sure is.
确实如此。

901
00:43:16.210 --> 00:43:22.510
And there is a joke right off the bat that was so funny to me, where Ryan is making plans
刚开始就有一个让我觉得特别好笑的梗，瑞安在计划

902
00:43:22.510 --> 00:43:29.350
for the weekend, and then he says, yeah, she's like a New York 6, but in Scranton, she's
周末的安排，然后他说，没错，她在纽约算6分，但在斯克兰顿，她

903
00:43:29.350 --> 00:43:29.770
a 7.
是7分。

904
00:43:30.450 --> 00:43:37.250
And then he says, and my boss is my old boss, which makes it very clear that the Scranton
接着他说，而且我的老板是我以前的老板，这让人很清楚地明白，斯克兰顿的

905
00:43:37.250 --> 00:43:39.730
7 is Pam in New York 6.
7分就是纽约的6分帕姆。

906
00:43:39.970 --> 00:43:40.050
Yeah.
没错。

907
00:43:40.050 --> 00:43:43.570
And they cut to you and your face as you realize it is so great.
然后镜头切到你，你意识到这一点时的表情真是太棒了。

908
00:43:44.170 --> 00:43:49.210
Justin said he felt like this was one of those amazing moments where the joke came before
贾斯汀说他觉得这是一个绝妙的时刻，笑话先于

909
00:43:49.210 --> 00:43:52.310
the setup and paid off in this amazing way.
铺垫出现，并以这种惊人的方式得到了回报。

910
00:43:52.430 --> 00:43:54.370
The whole thing is such a smart joke.
整个梗设计得太聪明了。

911
00:43:54.650 --> 00:43:56.310
It's so well-crafted.
制作得非常精良。

912
00:43:56.570 --> 00:43:57.850
It made me laugh.
它把我逗笑了。

913
00:43:57.950 --> 00:43:59.250
I absolutely loved it.
我真的太喜欢了。

914
00:43:59.590 --> 00:44:04.770
So I think we should stay down here in Michael Scott Paper Company and discuss the next thing
所以我觉得我们应该留在迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司，讨论接下来

