want to tell you a little bit about it.
想给你们讲讲它的来历。

921
00:44:24.230 --> 00:44:26.550
So this went viral in 2006.
这个视频在2006年走红。

922
00:44:26.910 --> 00:44:33.710
A man named Sammy Stevens created and wrote and performed a jingle for his Montgomery, Alabama
一个叫萨米·史蒂文斯的人为他在阿拉巴马州蒙哥马利的

923
00:44:33.710 --> 00:44:34.190
business.
生意创作、编写并演唱了一段广告歌。

924
00:44:34.190 --> 00:44:35.250
It was a flea market.
那是一家跳蚤市场。

925
00:44:35.470 --> 00:44:36.610
Oh, yeah.
哦，是吗。

926
00:44:36.610 --> 00:44:38.230
And he did his own commercial.
他自己拍了广告。

927
00:44:38.890 --> 00:44:40.630
And it went viral.
然后它就火了。

928
00:44:40.870 --> 00:44:43.210
Over 12 million people have watched this video.
超过1200万人观看了这个视频。

929
00:44:43.750 --> 00:44:46.830
Of course, it went viral before YouTube was kind of YouTube, right?
当然，它走红的时候YouTube还没完全成为现在的YouTube，对吧？

930
00:44:46.910 --> 00:44:47.850
And it wasn't monetized.
而且它没有被商业化。

931
00:44:47.970 --> 00:44:50.550
So he has said in interviews, he didn't make any money off of that.
所以他在采访中说，他没从那个视频里赚到一分钱。

932
00:44:50.650 --> 00:44:52.530
But it really took off.
但它确实火遍了全网。

933
00:44:52.650 --> 00:44:54.750
And Ellen DeGeneres had him on as a gueSt.
艾伦·德杰尼勒斯还邀请他做过嘉宾。

934
00:44:55.050 --> 00:44:55.350
Really?
真的吗？

935
00:44:55.690 --> 00:44:55.890
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

936
00:44:56.490 --> 00:44:58.410
The flea market is no longer in business.
那家跳蚤市场现在已经倒闭了。

937
00:44:58.570 --> 00:45:02.610
But Sammy is still writing commercial campaigns and performing.
但萨米还在创作广告活动并进行表演。

938
00:45:02.610 --> 00:45:05.110
He has appearances on TV and a radio show.
他还在电视和广播节目中露面。

939
00:45:05.290 --> 00:45:06.830
And I found Sammy on Instagram.
我在Instagram上找到了萨米。

940
00:45:07.190 --> 00:45:09.610
He's at TheRealSammyStevens.
他的账号是TheRealSammyStevens。

941
00:45:09.810 --> 00:45:11.530
S-T-E-P-H-E-N-S.
S-T-E-P-H-E-N-S。

942
00:45:11.530 --> 00:45:18.150
Something I love about our show is that we were always working in these pop culture topical
我喜欢我们剧的一点是，我们总是会融入这些流行文化的热点

943
00:45:18.150 --> 00:45:21.510
moments because that's what people do.
时刻，因为人们平时就是这样。

944
00:45:21.730 --> 00:45:25.770
That's what you would do is watch this YouTube video that was very popular while you were
你上班的时候肯定也会看这种当时很火的YouTube视频。

945
00:45:25.770 --> 00:45:26.150
at work.
这完全说得通。

946
00:45:26.290 --> 00:45:27.390
It makes total sense to me.
我完全理解。

947
00:45:27.570 --> 00:45:27.710
Yeah.
没错。

948
00:45:27.790 --> 00:45:29.210
And you would show all your co-workers.
而且你还会给所有同事看。

949
00:45:29.450 --> 00:45:31.350
It's actually something that would happen on our set.
这其实也是我们片场会发生的事情。

950
00:45:31.350 --> 00:45:35.910
As we've shared, Oscar had the only working computer with sound.
正如我们之前分享过的，奥斯卡当时是唯一拥有带声音的正常工作电脑的人。

951
00:45:35.910 --> 00:45:38.670
And we would all huddle around his computer and watch videos.
我们都会挤在他的电脑前看视频。

952
00:45:38.670 --> 00:45:45.410
Well, at seven minutes and five seconds, at the very top of the scene, you can see something
在七分零五秒，也就是这一幕刚开始的时候，你可以看到有个东西

953
00:45:45.410 --> 00:45:50.670
sitting next to Ryan in the little, like, poker chip caddy.
放在瑞安旁边那个类似筹码盒的小盒子里。

954
00:45:50.850 --> 00:45:51.090
Yeah.
没错。

955
00:45:51.450 --> 00:45:53.750
Because we're sitting at a poker table, which is amazing.
因为我们当时正坐在扑克桌旁，这太棒了。

956
00:45:54.350 --> 00:45:55.830
It is an inhaler.
那是一个吸入器。

957
00:45:56.290 --> 00:45:56.970
Yes.
是的。

958
00:45:56.970 --> 00:45:59.650
This was a whole deleted runner.
这原本是一整段被删减的剧情线。

959
00:45:59.870 --> 00:46:00.310
Yes.
是的。

960
00:46:00.570 --> 00:46:02.690
That Ryan uses an inhaler.
瑞安用吸入器那段。

961
00:46:03.370 --> 00:46:08.410
And he and Pam even get in a fight at one point, and she steals his inhaler.
而且有一点他和帕姆还吵了一架，她把他的吸入器偷走了。

962
00:46:08.610 --> 00:46:11.610
Well, because Michael, he hands it to Michael for Michael to use.
是因为迈克尔，他把吸入器递给迈克尔让他用。

963
00:46:11.710 --> 00:46:13.670
And she's like, wait, that might be bad for him.
然后帕姆就觉得，等等，这对迈克尔可能不好。

964
00:46:13.930 --> 00:46:14.130
Yeah.
没错。

965
00:46:14.250 --> 00:46:15.130
It's a whole thing.
这整件事挺复杂的。

966
00:46:15.250 --> 00:46:16.310
It ended up getting cut.
最后被剪掉了。

967
00:46:16.310 --> 00:46:18.470
But that's why there is this inhaler.
但这就是为什么那里会有个吸入器。

968
00:46:18.470 --> 00:46:22.750
And you can spot it throughout the episode sitting next to the laptop.
你可以在整集里看到它一直放在笔记本电脑旁边。

969
00:46:23.130 --> 00:46:29.410
There is also a fantastic shot at seven minutes, 36 seconds of all the clocks on the wall.
在七分三十六秒还有一个很棒的镜头，拍的是墙上的所有时钟。

970
00:46:30.090 --> 00:46:31.850
I think we have to talk about them.
我觉得我们得聊聊它们。

971
00:46:32.150 --> 00:46:36.810
There is a clock for Paris, London, Beijing, and the USA.
墙上有巴黎、伦敦、北京和美国的时间。

972
00:46:37.470 --> 00:46:43.290
According to Jean and Lee and Justin, the USA clock was set to Scranton.
据简、李和贾斯汀说，美国那个时钟设的是斯克兰顿的时间。

973
00:46:43.290 --> 00:46:49.950
But all the other clocks were set to the time interval between those cities and Los Angeles.
但其他所有时钟设的都是那些城市与洛杉矶之间的时间差。

974
00:46:51.390 --> 00:46:54.250
And they caught this error halfway through the episode.
他们在这一集播到一半时才发现这个错误。

975
00:46:54.250 --> 00:46:56.610
And they were just like, ah, we can't change it now.
他们当时就想，啊，现在改不了了。

976
00:46:56.730 --> 00:46:57.750
We have to just leave it.
只能就这么放着了。

977
00:46:57.910 --> 00:46:59.930
Oh, we got a lot of mail about those clocks, Angela.
噢，安吉拉，我们收到了很多关于那些时钟的来信。

978
00:47:00.090 --> 00:47:01.250
I'm very glad that you brought it up.
很高兴你提到了这一点。

979
00:47:01.470 --> 00:47:04.250
People will feel very satisfied because that has been spotted.
大家一定会感到很满足，因为终于有人发现了。

980
00:47:04.790 --> 00:47:12.030
You know, also in this scene, there is this very subtle thing that happens between Ryan and Pam that makes me laugh.
你知道吗，在这一幕里，瑞安和帕姆之间还有一个非常微妙的互动，让我觉得很好笑。

981
00:47:12.030 --> 00:47:15.030
And they're discussing who should make the copies.
当时他们在讨论该由谁去复印。

982
00:47:15.730 --> 00:47:18.530
And Ryan says, you're just so good at it.
瑞安说，你在这方面真的很擅长。

983
00:47:18.630 --> 00:47:19.890
You should do it, Pam.
你应该去做的，帕姆。

984
00:47:20.110 --> 00:47:24.510
And she's like, you're saying that what I'm good at is pressing a big green button.
然后她说，你的意思是说我擅长的事就是按那个大绿按钮？

985
00:47:25.290 --> 00:47:30.930
And he's kind of like, listen, I don't judge what we're good at.
他就像是说，听着，我不会去评判我们擅长什么。

986
00:47:31.050 --> 00:47:31.190
Yeah.
没错。

987
00:47:31.250 --> 00:47:33.910
He's like, why is it insulting to say that you're good at something?
他说，说你擅长某件事为什么就是侮辱呢？

988
00:47:34.190 --> 00:47:34.430
Yeah.
没错。

989
00:47:34.430 --> 00:47:49.330
So this reminded me of this very funny back and forth that my husband and I have had because I always say that Lee makes the best coffee in the morning and the best eggs.
这让我想起我和我丈夫之间一段非常有趣的对话，因为我总是说李早上做的咖啡最好喝，煎蛋也做得最好。

990
00:47:49.610 --> 00:47:52.830
And I guess I'm very complimentary about it.
我想我对他总是赞不绝口。

991
00:47:52.990 --> 00:47:54.690
I'm always like, these are the best eggs.
我总是说，这是最好吃的煎蛋。

992
00:47:54.950 --> 00:47:55.910
This is the best coffee.
这是最好喝的咖啡。

993
00:47:56.910 --> 00:48:05.730
So about like five years into our marriage, Lee says to me, do I really make the best eggs?
所以结婚大概五年后，李问我，我真的做得出最好的煎蛋吗？

994
00:48:06.250 --> 00:48:06.970
Five years?
五年？

995
00:48:07.090 --> 00:48:07.250
Yeah.
是的。

996
00:48:07.550 --> 00:48:09.030
He's been holding on to that.
他竟然憋了这么久。

997
00:48:11.620 --> 00:48:14.920
Do I really make the best coffee and the best eggs?
我真的做得出最好的咖啡和煎蛋吗？

998
00:48:15.000 --> 00:48:17.400
Or is it just that you don't want to make them?
还是说只是因为你不想做？

999
00:48:18.660 --> 00:48:20.560
And I was like, what?
我当时就惊了，什么？

1000
00:48:20.560 --> 00:48:27.720
And he said, I mean, how hard is it to make good coffee and eggs, really?
他说，我是说，做杯好咖啡和煎蛋到底能有多难？

1001
00:48:28.220 --> 00:48:29.160
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1002
00:48:29.420 --> 00:48:37.220
I feel like maybe you're just complimenting my coffee and eggs so that I make you coffee and eggs every day.
我觉得你可能只是为了让我每天都给你做咖啡和煎蛋，才夸我的咖啡和煎蛋好喝。

1003
00:48:38.200 --> 00:48:42.520
And I was like, no, they really are superior.
我当时就说，不，它们确实更胜一筹。

1004
00:48:42.520 --> 00:48:45.280
I swear it's better coffee than I make.
我发誓这咖啡比我做的要好喝。

1005
00:48:45.280 --> 00:48:52.220
I mean, that we could prove because there were some mornings when I made the coffee and Lee was like, oh, yeah, that's not great.
我是说，这一点我们可以证明，因为有些早上是我做的咖啡，李就会说，噢，好吧，这咖啡不怎么样。

1006
00:48:52.320 --> 00:48:54.040
But Lee doesn't eat eggs.
但李不吃鸡蛋。

1007
00:48:54.200 --> 00:48:57.460
I eat eggs in the morning and he would always make me my eggs.
我早上吃鸡蛋，他总是会帮我做。

1008
00:48:57.520 --> 00:48:59.020
But it's the truth, babe.
但这是真的，亲爱的。

1009
00:48:59.460 --> 00:49:01.980
Lee, you make the best coffee and eggs.
李，你做的咖啡和煎蛋是最好的。

1010
00:49:02.160 --> 00:49:03.280
You just do.
你就是做得最好。

1011
00:49:04.120 --> 00:49:07.640
Lee, I've traveled only a handful of times with your wife.
李，我和你妻子一起旅行的次数屈指可数。

1012
00:49:07.860 --> 00:49:10.320
I know you have traveled with her many, many times.
我知道你和她一起旅行过很多很多次。

1013
00:49:11.100 --> 00:49:14.520
And I know that this woman does not lie about food or beverage.
而且我知道这个女人在食物或饮料方面从不撒谎。

1014
00:49:14.520 --> 00:49:15.380
Thank you.
谢谢。

1015
00:49:15.800 --> 00:49:18.540
She is completely earnest when she likes something.
当她喜欢某样东西时，她是完全真诚的。

1016
00:49:18.660 --> 00:49:20.500
And when she doesn't, you're going to know about it.
而当她不喜欢时，你一定会知道。

1017
00:49:20.680 --> 00:49:21.420
That's the thing.
就是这样。

1018
00:49:21.580 --> 00:49:28.020
I'm not going to eat mediocre eggs for five years just because someone else made them for me.
我才不会为了让别人帮我做饭，就连续五年吃平庸的煎蛋。

1019
00:49:28.060 --> 00:49:32.200
I mean, if I really believed I could make better eggs, I'd be making my own eggs.
我是说，如果我真的相信自己能做出更好的煎蛋，我早就自己做了。

1020
00:49:32.300 --> 00:49:32.560
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

1021
00:49:32.760 --> 00:49:38.540
Well, once again, while people are talking in Michael Scott Paper Company, you hear someone in the bathroom.
好吧，再一次，当人们在迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司谈话时，你会听到洗手间里有人。

1022
00:49:38.880 --> 00:49:42.140
Yeah, you hear their voice through the ceiling.
没错，你能通过天花板听到他们的声音。

1023
00:49:42.140 --> 00:49:44.080
You hear them peeing.
你能听到他们撒尿的声音。

1024
00:49:44.440 --> 00:49:47.060
We had a fan question from Afrin R.
我们收到了一个来自Afrin R.的粉丝提问。

1025
00:49:47.400 --> 00:49:54.920
In the scene where Michael, Pam, and Ryan are in their small new office and we hear a male voice talking on his phone in the bathroom.
在迈克尔、帕姆和瑞安在他们狭小的新办公室里的那场戏中，我们听到洗手间里有一个男声在打电话。

1026
00:49:55.060 --> 00:49:55.920
Whose voice is it?
那是谁的声音？

1027
00:49:56.020 --> 00:49:59.540
It sounds like Toby, but the conversation made me doubt it.
听起来像托比，但谈话内容让我产生了怀疑。

1028
00:49:59.960 --> 00:50:01.280
It was Toby.
那是托比。

1029
00:50:01.900 --> 00:50:02.960
Paul did the voice.
保罗配的音。

1030
00:50:02.960 --> 00:50:10.180
Now, on the commentary, I think Gene and Lee joked that they made Paul sit up in the ceiling tiles to do his lines.
现在，在评论音轨里，我想吉恩和李开玩笑说他们让保罗坐在天花板瓷砖上念台词。

1031
00:50:10.940 --> 00:50:12.060
But that is not true.
但那不是真的。

1032
00:50:12.260 --> 00:50:14.140
He was actually just off camera.
他实际上就在镜头外。

1033
00:50:14.140 --> 00:50:15.320
He was not in the ceiling.
他并没有在天花板里。

1034
00:50:15.720 --> 00:50:22.240
They added all the effects in post to make it sound like he was in the bathroom above us, including, like, all the peeing sounds.
他们在后期制作中添加了所有效果，让声音听起来像是在我们头顶的洗手间里，包括所有的撒尿声。

1035
00:50:22.380 --> 00:50:24.360
But it really sounds like he's above you.
但听起来真的很像他在你们头顶上。

1036
00:50:24.460 --> 00:50:26.440
I mean, I was so sold on that.
我是说，我完全被骗到了。

1037
00:50:26.600 --> 00:50:26.820
Yeah.
没错。

1038
00:50:26.820 --> 00:50:27.920
No, he was not.
不，他不在那儿。

1039
00:50:28.120 --> 00:50:29.140
He was just off camera.
他只是在镜头外。

1040
00:50:29.440 --> 00:50:41.040
But incidentally, I would like to point out that our sound team was nominated for an Emmy for Outstanding Sound Mixing for a Comedy or Drama Series Half Hour for this episode.
但顺便提一下，我想指出我们的音效团队凭借这一集获得了艾美奖半小时喜剧或剧情类剧集最佳音效混音提名。

1041
00:50:41.240 --> 00:50:42.320
Well, they deserve it.
嗯，他们实至名归。

1042
00:50:42.420 --> 00:50:42.840
I know.
我知道。

1043
00:50:42.940 --> 00:50:44.680
It really sounded like he was up there.
听起来真的像他在上面一样。

1044
00:50:44.780 --> 00:50:46.220
And all the flushing and everything.
还有所有的冲水声和一切声音。

1045
00:50:47.200 --> 00:50:52.620
Well, Michael's going to call his mom and talk in code, Jenna, much in the way that you and I talk in code.
好吧，迈克尔要给他妈妈打电话并用暗语交谈，珍娜，就像你我用暗语交谈一样。

1046
00:50:52.760 --> 00:50:53.780
He's really bad at it.
他在这方面真的很差劲。

1047
00:50:54.000 --> 00:50:54.900
It's so obvious.
太明显了。

1048
00:50:55.080 --> 00:50:55.600
It's so obvious.
太明显了。

1049
00:50:55.800 --> 00:50:58.020
He says, Mom, they're getting on my nerves.
他说，妈，他们让我很心烦。

1050
00:50:58.240 --> 00:50:59.580
R thinks he's too good to be here.
R觉得他太优秀了，不屑于待在这里。

1051
00:50:59.680 --> 00:51:01.660
And P is not as much fun without Jim.
而且没有了吉姆，帕姆也没那么有趣了。

1052
00:51:02.120 --> 00:51:04.140
And then he's like, Mom, I got to go.
然后他说，妈，我得走了。

1053
00:51:04.280 --> 00:51:05.440
P's being a giant bee.
帕姆在装一只大蜜蜂。

1054
00:51:06.140 --> 00:51:07.260
This is us, lady.
这就是我们，女士。

1055
00:51:07.640 --> 00:51:13.800
Well, this whole thing is going to end with Pam and Ryan bickering over the computer.
整件事最后肯定会演变成帕姆和瑞安为了电脑争吵不休。

1056
00:51:13.800 --> 00:51:17.500
I mean, they get in a huge fight over who gets to use it.
我是说，他们会为了谁能用电脑大吵一架。

1057
00:51:17.940 --> 00:51:24.120
And at eight minutes and 20 seconds at the end of this scene, the camera pushes in on Michael.
在这一幕结束时，也就是八分二十秒处，镜头推向了迈克尔。

1058
00:51:24.600 --> 00:51:26.300
He's standing in front of the whiteboard.
他正站在白板前。

1059
00:51:26.560 --> 00:51:33.380
And written on the whiteboard is a quote that says, you miss 100% of the shots.
白板上写着一句引言，说你错失了百分之百的投篮。

1060
00:51:33.660 --> 00:51:34.300
You don't take.
那些你没投的。

1061
00:51:34.600 --> 00:51:36.920
Wayne Gretzky, Michael Scott.
韦恩·格雷茨基，迈克尔·斯科特。

1062
00:51:38.360 --> 00:51:41.100
As if Wayne Gretzky is part of the quote.
就好像韦恩·格雷茨基也是那句引言的一部分一样。

1063
00:51:41.380 --> 00:51:41.940
Yes.
没错。

1064
00:51:42.280 --> 00:51:42.460
Right?
对吧？

1065
00:51:42.460 --> 00:51:46.940
Michael Scott is quoting himself, quoting Wayne Gretzky.
迈克尔·斯科特是在引用他自己，而他引用的是韦恩·格雷茨基。

1066
00:51:47.480 --> 00:51:49.500
Justin Spitzer wrote that joke.
贾斯汀·斯皮策写了这个笑话。

1067
00:51:50.060 --> 00:51:54.820
Gene and Lee both brought it up, saying it was one of their favorite parts of the episode.
吉恩和李都提到了这一点，说这是他们最喜欢的一集片段之一。

1068
00:51:55.160 --> 00:51:57.500
Like, I see that meme all the time.
我经常看到那个梗图。

1069
00:51:57.720 --> 00:51:58.280
Oh, yeah.
噢，确实。

1070
00:51:58.460 --> 00:51:59.180
It's so brilliant.
太天才了。

1071
00:51:59.400 --> 00:52:06.600
If you Google Wayne Gretzky's quote, a Michael Scott version with his picture comes up.
如果你在谷歌上搜索韦恩·格雷茨基的引言，会出现迈克尔·斯科特版本的配图。

1072
00:52:06.700 --> 00:52:07.220
It's crazy.
太疯狂了。

1073
00:52:07.220 --> 00:52:09.020
Well, why don't we take a break?
好吧，我们休息一下怎么样？

1074
00:52:09.240 --> 00:52:21.480
And when we come back, we still have to discuss the pancake luncheon and Dwight and Andy's rivalry and Jim maybe finally figuring out what a rundown is.
回来之后，我们还要讨论煎饼午餐、德怀特和安迪的竞争，以及吉姆可能终于弄明白什么是工作进度表了。

1075
00:52:21.620 --> 00:52:25.200
And also a scene where maybe Jim has disappeared.
还有一幕是吉姆可能消失了。

1076
00:52:25.580 --> 00:52:26.540
Where has he gone?
他去哪儿了？

1077
00:52:26.540 --> 00:52:27.920
And you might have the answer.
也许你有答案。

1078
00:52:28.160 --> 00:52:28.760
Oh, wow.
噢，哇。

1079
00:52:28.980 --> 00:52:31.080
Oh, I also have a sunglasses thing.
噢，我还有个关于太阳镜的事要说。

1080
00:52:31.320 --> 00:52:32.700
Oh, and I do too.
噢，我也有。

1081
00:52:32.940 --> 00:52:34.620
There's so much to come back for.
后面还有很多精彩内容。

1082
00:52:44.030 --> 00:52:44.890
We're back.
我们回来了。

1083
00:52:45.350 --> 00:52:50.450
Dwight is going to approach Andy about his obvious attraction to Aaron.
德怀特打算找安迪谈谈他对艾琳明显的爱慕之情。

1084
00:52:50.450 --> 00:52:56.530
And only a way that Dwight would, about tingly feelings and blood flow to places.
而且是以德怀特特有的方式，谈论什么酥麻的感觉和血液流向某些部位。

1085
00:52:57.490 --> 00:52:57.750
Yes.
是的。

1086
00:52:58.030 --> 00:53:02.770
But he also confesses that he has his own feelings for Aaron.
但他同时也承认自己对艾琳也有感觉。

1087
00:53:03.370 --> 00:53:03.770
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1088
00:53:04.210 --> 00:53:08.130
And they sort of talk about like, no, no, no, I don't want to get in your way and vice versa.
他们大概是这样说的，不，不，不，我不想挡你的路，反之亦然。

1089
00:53:08.350 --> 00:53:08.610
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1090
00:53:08.610 --> 00:53:18.370
I want you to note at 9 minutes, 28 seconds, while Dwight and Andy are talking, Aaron is in the background directly in the middle of these two guys.
我想请大家注意九分二十八秒处，当德怀特和安迪交谈时，艾琳就在背景里，正好处于这两个人中间。

1091
00:53:18.930 --> 00:53:20.690
Oh, I'm sure that was on purpose.
噢，我敢肯定那是故意的。

1092
00:53:21.010 --> 00:53:21.750
Oh, it was.
噢，确实是。

1093
00:53:21.950 --> 00:53:23.730
Gene and Lee said that was intentional.
吉恩和李说那是刻意安排的。

1094
00:53:24.250 --> 00:53:32.010
They said they did this as many times as they could in this episode because it is a story about a woman coming between two guys.
他们说在这一集中尽可能多地安排了这样的画面，因为这是一个关于女人介入两个男人之间的故事。

1095
00:53:32.470 --> 00:53:38.370
I really loved Leslie's look in the background as well.
我也非常喜欢莱斯利在背景里的表情。

1096
00:53:38.370 --> 00:53:40.270
There's a lot to see in the background of this scene.
这一幕的背景里有很多值得看的东西。

1097
00:53:40.390 --> 00:53:41.010
That's pretty great.
那真是太棒了。

1098
00:53:41.230 --> 00:53:44.110
And there's also someone missing in the background of this scene.
而且这一幕的背景里还少了一个人。

1099
00:53:44.970 --> 00:53:45.970
Where is Jim?
吉姆在哪儿？

1100
00:53:46.390 --> 00:53:47.250
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1101
00:53:47.650 --> 00:53:49.110
I can tell you where he was.
我可以告诉你他在哪儿。

1102
00:53:49.250 --> 00:53:49.910
Where was he?
他在哪儿？

1103
00:53:50.170 --> 00:53:54.250
They shared in the commentary that John had to leave early to be on The Tonight Show.
他们在评论音轨里提到，约翰得早退去参加《今夜秀》。

1104
00:53:54.450 --> 00:53:55.550
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1105
00:53:56.790 --> 00:54:04.310
Well, you know, we were rapidly approaching our 100th episode of The Office, which is going to be Company Picnic, the finale of Season 5.
嗯，你知道，我们当时快要拍到《办公室》的第100集了，也就是第五季的季终集《公司野餐》。

1106
00:54:04.610 --> 00:54:08.050
And we were starting to do a lot of press and promotion for that.
我们开始为那一集做大量的媒体宣传。

1107
00:54:08.370 --> 00:54:20.390
I saw on the call sheets that after work on Thursday of this week, me and John and Rain stayed after work, and we shot some syndicated promos.
我在通告单上看到，这周四下班后，我和约翰还有雷恩留下来拍了一些联合推广视频。

1108
00:54:21.230 --> 00:54:21.710
Oh, yeah.
哦，是吗。

1109
00:54:22.110 --> 00:54:26.830
I found some old emails that a few of us did a satellite media tour as well.
我翻到了一些旧邮件，我们几个还参加了卫星媒体巡回采访。

1110
00:54:26.990 --> 00:54:27.510
I bet.
我敢肯定。

1111
00:54:27.510 --> 00:54:27.850
Yeah.
没错。

1112
00:54:28.110 --> 00:54:34.370
I always got roped in for those, and they started at 4 in the morning because you do East Coast to West CoaSt.
我总是被拉去参加这些活动，它们通常凌晨4点就开始，因为要从东海岸一直连线到西海岸。

1113
00:54:34.650 --> 00:54:35.950
We were very excited.
我们当时非常兴奋。

1114
00:54:35.950 --> 00:54:37.110
We were happy to do it.
我们很乐意去做。

1115
00:54:37.210 --> 00:54:38.110
We were team players.
我们很有团队精神。

1116
00:54:38.390 --> 00:54:40.710
I was always really proud of our group effort for the show.
我一直为我们团队为这部剧付出的努力感到自豪。

1117
00:54:41.930 --> 00:54:48.430
Well, Jim is going to reappear pretty quickly because he's asking Oscar what the rundown is, right?
吉姆很快就会再次出现，因为他在问奥斯卡“工作摘要”是什么，对吧？

1118
00:54:48.570 --> 00:54:48.790
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1119
00:54:48.790 --> 00:54:52.290
He's gone over to the accounting nook much of the way that Michael used to do.
他走到会计部的小隔间里，就像迈克尔以前常做的那样。

1120
00:54:52.290 --> 00:54:57.330
He would go ask Oscar what something meant, and now Jim is doing it.
迈克尔以前会去问奥斯卡某个词是什么意思，现在轮到吉姆了。

1121
00:54:57.450 --> 00:55:00.230
I mean, Oscar's kind of the smartest guy in the office.
我是说，奥斯卡算是办公室里最聪明的人了。

1122
00:55:00.450 --> 00:55:05.010
Jenna, I love that you said that because Justin Spitzer said this in the commentary.
珍娜，我很高兴你这么说，因为贾斯汀·斯皮策在评论音轨里也这么说过。

1123
00:55:05.270 --> 00:55:08.730
He joked that Oscar was the voice of the writers.
他开玩笑说奥斯卡就是编剧们的代言人。

1124
00:55:09.070 --> 00:55:12.190
He's the smartest guy who's always judging everyone.
他是最聪明的人，而且总是在评判每个人。

1125
00:55:15.680 --> 00:55:16.800
Yeah, 100%.
没错，百分之百。

1126
00:55:16.800 --> 00:55:19.320
But Oscar says, why don't you just ask him?
但奥斯卡说，你为什么不直接去问他呢？

1127
00:55:19.500 --> 00:55:22.060
Just ask Charles what the rundown is.
直接去问查尔斯“工作摘要”是什么。

1128
00:55:22.920 --> 00:55:27.860
So there was a deleted scene where Jim actually took Oscar's advice.
所以有一个被删减的片段，吉姆真的听取了奥斯卡的建议。

1129
00:55:28.060 --> 00:55:28.240
What?
什么？

1130
00:55:28.560 --> 00:55:28.940
Yeah.
是的。

1131
00:55:29.240 --> 00:55:30.180
You've got to hear it.
你一定要听听看。

1132
00:55:32.860 --> 00:55:33.300
You have a second?
你有空吗？

1133
00:55:33.860 --> 00:55:34.560
What is it, Jim?
什么事，吉姆？

1134
00:55:34.820 --> 00:55:36.020
It's about the rundown.
是关于工作摘要的事。

1135
00:55:36.400 --> 00:55:40.840
Jim, God, this rundown is taking more of my time than if I did it myself.
吉姆，天哪，这份工作摘要花掉我的时间比我自己做还要多。

1136
00:55:40.840 --> 00:55:41.280
What?
什么？

1137
00:55:41.920 --> 00:55:43.280
What is the question now?
现在又有什么问题？

1138
00:55:44.080 --> 00:55:45.020
What's a rundown?
什么是工作摘要？

1139
00:55:47.200 --> 00:55:48.440
Is this one of your pranks?
这是你的恶作剧之一吗？

1140
00:55:52.420 --> 00:55:52.940
Huh?
啊？

1141
00:55:54.660 --> 00:55:55.020
Yep.
没错。

1142
00:55:57.000 --> 00:55:57.360
Boom.
砰。

1143
00:55:57.620 --> 00:55:57.800
Jim.
吉姆。

1144
00:55:58.100 --> 00:55:58.380
Sorry.
抱歉。

1145
00:55:58.560 --> 00:55:59.080
I don't have time.
我没时间。

1146
00:55:59.180 --> 00:55:59.400
I know.
我知道。

1147
00:55:59.540 --> 00:55:59.720
Okay.
好吧。

1148
00:55:59.900 --> 00:56:00.120
All right.
行吧。

1149
00:56:00.380 --> 00:56:01.340
I'm going to get you that rundown.
我会把那份工作摘要拿给你的。

1150
00:56:01.340 --> 00:56:02.000
Just give it to me, Jim.
直接给我吧，吉姆。

1151
00:56:02.140 --> 00:56:02.440
Right now.
就在现在。

1152
00:56:02.700 --> 00:56:05.200
I'm going to go out and find it.
我要出去把它找出来。

1153
00:56:06.140 --> 00:56:07.320
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1154
00:56:07.560 --> 00:56:08.500
Isn't that amazing?
那不是很神奇吗？

1155
00:56:08.920 --> 00:56:13.660
And I love that Charles clearly knows that Jim's the prankster, which he probably, you
我喜欢查尔斯显然知道吉姆就是那个恶作剧者，他可能，你知道，

1156
00:56:13.660 --> 00:56:16.320
know, just add that to the list of things he doesn't like about Jim.
把这一点加到他不喜欢吉姆的事情清单里。

1157
00:56:16.720 --> 00:56:19.900
But Jim actually asked him and then bailed.
但吉姆确实问过他，然后又临阵脱逃了。

1158
00:56:20.800 --> 00:56:22.380
I bet that was a really funny scene.
我敢打赌那一定是个非常有趣的场景。

1159
00:56:22.400 --> 00:56:23.440
I wish that had stayed in.
真希望那段没被剪掉。

1160
00:56:23.940 --> 00:56:24.400
It was great.
那太棒了。

1161
00:56:24.500 --> 00:56:27.420
There was so much awkward, just long pauses.
当时有好多尴尬的、漫长的停顿。

1162
00:56:27.760 --> 00:56:27.960
Oh.
噢。

1163
00:56:28.580 --> 00:56:33.300
Well, back downstairs, Michael determines that their office space is too small.
回到楼下，迈克尔认定他们的办公空间太小了。

1164
00:56:34.200 --> 00:56:38.280
He says that the solution is for Pam and Ryan to each choose a corner.
他说解决方案是让帕姆和瑞安各自选一个角落。

1165
00:56:38.800 --> 00:56:40.820
Pam suggests they work from home.
帕姆建议他们在家办公。

1166
00:56:41.140 --> 00:56:44.500
Ryan suggests Michael fire whichever of them has less education.
瑞安建议迈克尔解雇他们中受教育程度较低的那个人。

1167
00:56:44.840 --> 00:56:47.200
There's a little bit of that passive aggressive.
这带有一点点消极攻击的意味。

1168
00:56:47.200 --> 00:56:50.820
But Michael is like, no, my corner idea is what it is.
但迈克尔坚持说，不，我的角落方案就是这样。

1169
00:56:51.120 --> 00:56:57.560
I want you to know there was a talking head in the script where Michael says that he negotiated
我想让你知道，剧本里有一个采访镜头，迈克尔说他为这个空间

1170
00:56:57.560 --> 00:56:59.640
a seven-year lease on this space.
谈下了一份七年的租约。

1171
00:56:59.640 --> 00:57:00.160
No.
不。

1172
00:57:01.580 --> 00:57:02.220
No.
不。

1173
00:57:02.740 --> 00:57:03.660
But it gets worse.
但情况更糟。

1174
00:57:03.960 --> 00:57:07.540
He says, originally, Billy started at three years.
他说，最初，比利提出的是三年。

1175
00:57:07.760 --> 00:57:09.640
Michael countered with seven.
迈克尔还价到七年。

1176
00:57:09.780 --> 00:57:10.780
No, Michael.
不，迈克尔。

1177
00:57:11.140 --> 00:57:13.260
And then Michael says, I should have said 10.
然后迈克尔说，我当时应该说十年的。

1178
00:57:13.900 --> 00:57:15.040
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1179
00:57:15.040 --> 00:57:18.840
So, this is going to be their space for seven years.
所以，这就是他们未来七年的办公空间了。

1180
00:57:19.540 --> 00:57:21.100
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1181
00:57:21.600 --> 00:57:23.120
Justin pointed out something really funny.
贾斯汀指出了一个非常有趣的地方。

1182
00:57:23.300 --> 00:57:26.960
He was like, you know, when Michael says, there are four corners in this room.
他说，你知道，当迈克尔说，这个房间有四个角落时。

1183
00:57:27.100 --> 00:57:27.300
Yeah.
是啊。

1184
00:57:27.580 --> 00:57:29.600
And you guys kind of look to camera like, yeah, idiot.
你们几个对着镜头那种眼神，就像在说，是啊，白痴。

1185
00:57:30.420 --> 00:57:32.440
Actually, there were more than four.
实际上，角落不止四个。

1186
00:57:32.720 --> 00:57:36.480
There were because there were some, like, weird bumpy things.
确实不止，因为还有一些奇怪的凸起物。

1187
00:57:38.380 --> 00:57:40.780
Well, Pam is going to retreat to her corner.
好吧，帕姆准备退到她的角落里去。

1188
00:57:41.000 --> 00:57:45.680
By the way, her corner is next to the sewage pipe and the shower.
顺便说一下，她的角落就在污水管和淋浴间旁边。

1189
00:57:45.900 --> 00:57:47.120
Facing a wall.
面对着一堵墙。

1190
00:57:47.300 --> 00:57:49.060
You'd think it can't get worse.
你以为情况不会更糟了。

1191
00:57:49.600 --> 00:57:52.420
Ryan's corner is, like, behind a plant.
瑞安的角落，就像是在一株植物后面。

1192
00:57:52.420 --> 00:57:55.120
It's actually kind of the nicest corner, really.
实际上那算是最好的角落了，真的。

1193
00:57:55.880 --> 00:57:59.460
But things are going to get worse for Pam because Michael says that's his corner.
但帕姆的情况要变得更糟了，因为迈克尔说那是他的角落。

1194
00:57:59.600 --> 00:58:03.420
Because he can't work in the same corner that he relaxes in.
因为他不能在休息的角落里工作。

1195
00:58:03.520 --> 00:58:03.720
Right.
没错。

1196
00:58:04.040 --> 00:58:05.480
So, she's like, which one's mine?
所以她问，那哪个是我的？

1197
00:58:05.500 --> 00:58:07.640
And he says, yours is the one over there.
他说，你的在那边。

1198
00:58:07.880 --> 00:58:09.220
By the copier.
复印机旁边。

1199
00:58:09.380 --> 00:58:09.740
Oh.
噢。

1200
00:58:09.980 --> 00:58:14.040
We had a fan catch at 12 minutes, one second.
我们在12分01秒处有一个粉丝发现的穿帮镜头。

1201
00:58:14.320 --> 00:58:16.600
And it's a great continuity catch.
这是一个很棒的连贯性漏洞发现。

1202
00:58:16.600 --> 00:58:17.720
It's very subtle.
非常细微。

1203
00:58:18.040 --> 00:58:25.240
So, hats off to Tatiana V, who says, when Pam goes to sit in her corner, she takes a small
所以，向Tatiana V致敬，她说，当帕姆去角落坐下时，她带了一个小的

1204
00:58:25.240 --> 00:58:26.760
black object with her.
黑色物体。

1205
00:58:26.760 --> 00:58:31.660
You can see her holding it in her lap as the camera swings back and forth from her and
当镜头在帕姆和迈克尔之间来回切换时，你可以看到她把它抱在膝盖上。

1206
00:58:31.660 --> 00:58:32.020
Michael.
迈克尔。

1207
00:58:33.620 --> 00:58:39.600
But, right before she gets up to leave, it has disappeared from her hands because Pam
但是，就在她起身离开之前，它从她手中消失了，因为帕姆

1208
00:58:39.600 --> 00:58:41.660
is now holding the arms of her chair.
现在正抓着椅子的扶手。

1209
00:58:41.980 --> 00:58:42.860
What is it?
那是什么？

1210
00:58:43.080 --> 00:58:44.580
That's what she wanted to know.
这就是她想知道的。

1211
00:58:44.760 --> 00:58:46.700
It was Pam's flip phone.
那是帕姆的翻盖手机。

1212
00:58:47.160 --> 00:58:52.620
Pam grabs her flip phone off of the poker table, but clearly I didn't do it in every take
帕姆从扑克桌上拿走了她的翻盖手机，但显然我并不是在每次拍摄时都做了这个动作，

1213
00:58:52.620 --> 00:58:54.580
because it does just vanish.
因为它确实就这样消失了。

1214
00:58:55.180 --> 00:58:56.460
I miss my flip phone.
我怀念我的翻盖手机。

1215
00:58:57.140 --> 00:58:57.760
You do?
真的吗？

1216
00:58:57.960 --> 00:58:58.380
I do.
是的。

1217
00:58:58.500 --> 00:59:02.980
And I miss the little antenna it had and how I would close the antenna with my chin.
我怀念它上面的小天线，以及我如何用下巴把天线合上。

1218
00:59:03.160 --> 00:59:04.620
I'd like shove it into my chin.
我会把它顶在下巴上。

1219
00:59:05.180 --> 00:59:06.720
It did feel fun.
感觉确实很有趣。

1220
00:59:07.000 --> 00:59:07.840
I loved it.
我喜欢它。

1221
00:59:07.980 --> 00:59:08.030
The flip phone.
翻盖手机。

1222
00:59:08.180 --> 00:59:08.340
Yeah.
是啊。

1223
00:59:08.840 --> 00:59:13.820
Well, you know, Samsung has a new flip phone thing where you flip it open and it becomes
嗯，你知道，三星有一款新的翻盖手机，你把它翻开，它就变成

1224
00:59:13.820 --> 00:59:14.820
like a big screen.
像一个大屏幕一样。

1225
00:59:14.820 --> 00:59:16.260
Have you seen the commercials for it?
你看过它的广告吗？

1226
00:59:16.260 --> 00:59:17.420
I'll never be able to figure it out.
我永远也搞不懂它。

1227
00:59:17.580 --> 00:59:18.540
There's too many moving parts.
活动的部件太多了。

1228
00:59:18.540 --> 00:59:20.540
I know, but it looks cool in the commercials.
我知道，但在广告里看起来很酷。

1229
00:59:20.540 --> 00:59:21.760
It really does, Samsung.
确实如此，三星。

1230
00:59:22.280 --> 00:59:24.400
You know what I don't miss about my flip phone, lady?
你知道我不怀念翻盖手机的哪一点吗，女士？

1231
00:59:24.660 --> 00:59:24.920
What?
什么？

1232
00:59:25.160 --> 00:59:28.300
I don't miss the texting where you had to...
我不怀念那种发短信的方式，你必须……

1233
00:59:28.300 --> 00:59:31.460
A-A-B-B-C-C-D-E-E.
A-A-B-B-C-C-D-E-E。

1234
00:59:31.600 --> 00:59:32.820
Like you had to click, click, click.
就像你必须点点点一样。

1235
00:59:32.880 --> 00:59:32.930
Yeah.
是啊。

1236
00:59:34.060 --> 00:59:40.820
Listen, all of this business with Ryan and the corners, Pam's going to leave.
听着，所有关于瑞安和角落的事情，帕姆要离开了。

1237
00:59:41.080 --> 00:59:45.060
She goes upstairs and she asks Charles for her old job back.
她上楼去问查尔斯能不能要回她的旧工作。

1238
00:59:45.280 --> 00:59:47.380
She doesn't consult her fiance.
她没有咨询她的未婚夫。

1239
00:59:48.100 --> 00:59:50.380
Not that she needs to consult him, but you know what I mean?
并不是说她需要咨询他，但你懂我的意思吗？

1240
00:59:50.400 --> 00:59:51.680
You would think she'd loop him in.
你本以为她会让他知情的。

1241
00:59:51.820 --> 00:59:54.820
You'd think she'd like say, Jim, I'm going to ask for my job back.
你本以为她会说，吉姆，我要去要回我的工作了。

1242
00:59:55.160 --> 00:59:59.160
But she didn't consult him when she quit and she's not going to consult him now.
但她辞职时没有咨询他，现在她也不会咨询他。

1243
00:59:59.380 --> 01:00:00.160
She's desperate.
她绝望了。

1244
01:00:00.340 --> 01:00:01.800
She doesn't have time for that conversation.
她没有时间进行那种对话。

1245
01:00:02.020 --> 01:00:02.160
No.
没有。

1246
01:00:02.760 --> 01:00:04.700
Well, Charles says the position has been filled.
嗯，查尔斯说那个职位已经有人了。

1247
01:00:05.100 --> 01:00:06.820
She says maybe a sales job.
她说也许销售工作也行。

1248
01:00:07.120 --> 01:00:10.360
Maybe a job as his personal assistant, personal shopper.
也许是做他的私人助理，私人采购员。

1249
01:00:11.300 --> 01:00:11.700
Nope.
不行。

1250
01:00:12.160 --> 01:00:12.860
No dice.
没戏。

1251
01:00:12.860 --> 01:00:20.300
So Justin talked about several different alts in the scene where they had Charles be really
贾斯汀谈到了几个不同的备选方案，在查尔斯对帕姆表现得非常

1252
01:00:20.300 --> 01:00:26.380
sort of abrupt with Pam and they dialed it back because it seemed too harsh.
生硬的那场戏里，他们后来调低了程度，因为看起来太刻薄了。

1253
01:00:26.560 --> 01:00:27.760
So he's just more indifferent.
所以他只是表现得更冷漠一些。

1254
01:00:28.040 --> 01:00:28.820
He's just more business.
他只是更公事公办。

1255
01:00:29.560 --> 01:00:29.720
Yeah.
是啊。

1256
01:00:29.940 --> 01:00:36.260
Well, this was my only real one-on-one scene with Idris, except for when he sort of came in
嗯，这是我唯一真正和伊德里斯一对一的戏份，除了他刚来

1257
01:00:36.260 --> 01:00:38.640
the first day, but that wasn't much of an exchange.
第一天的时候，但那次没怎么交流。

1258
01:00:39.400 --> 01:00:40.740
I was so nervous.
我当时太紧张了。

1259
01:00:41.540 --> 01:00:42.780
I was such a fan.
我是他的超级粉丝。

1260
01:00:43.600 --> 01:00:49.620
And to be standing there with this actor that I admired so much, because I was a huge fan of The Wire.
能和这位我非常钦佩的演员站在一起，因为我是《火线》的忠实粉丝。

1261
01:00:49.880 --> 01:00:54.360
And he has such a patient, quiet power in his scenes.
他在戏里有一种耐心而安静的力量感。

1262
01:00:54.460 --> 01:00:54.720
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1263
01:00:55.180 --> 01:00:56.540
And he's such a pro.
而且他非常专业。

1264
01:00:56.540 --> 01:01:04.720
So, I mean, I was just, I think some of my nervousness as Pam was just my nervousness as
所以，我的意思是，我想我作为帕姆表现出的一些紧张，其实就是我作为

1265
01:01:04.720 --> 01:01:07.120
Jenna performing with this person that I admired.
珍娜在和这位我钦佩的人演戏时的紧张。

1266
01:01:07.500 --> 01:01:07.720
Yeah.
是啊。

1267
01:01:08.220 --> 01:01:12.420
Word has clearly gotten out about the Michael Scott Paper Company being downstairs, because
迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司在楼下的消息显然已经传开了，因为

1268
01:01:12.420 --> 01:01:16.240
Phyllis and Stanley decide to go pop by and say hi.
菲利斯和斯坦利决定去顺道打个招呼。

1269
01:01:16.360 --> 01:01:17.500
We really know what it was.
我们其实知道是怎么回事。

1270
01:01:17.640 --> 01:01:18.560
They were just snooping.
他们只是在打探消息。

1271
01:01:19.220 --> 01:01:20.060
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

1272
01:01:20.160 --> 01:01:20.320
Yeah.
是啊。

1273
01:01:20.440 --> 01:01:21.320
I would do the same thing.
我也会做同样的事。

1274
01:01:21.320 --> 01:01:21.840
Are you kidding?
开什么玩笑？

1275
01:01:21.840 --> 01:01:28.720
Well, at the top of the scene, when Phyllis and Stanley poked their head in, I want you
嗯，在这一幕开始时，当菲利斯和斯坦利探头进来时，我希望你们

1276
01:01:28.720 --> 01:01:31.960
to notice that Michael is playing with the stapler.
注意到迈克尔正在玩那个订书机。

1277
01:01:32.560 --> 01:01:36.880
The stapler that we loved, that none of us could keep our hands off of.
那个我们都很喜欢的订书机，我们谁都忍不住想去碰它。

1278
01:01:37.020 --> 01:01:41.940
We would seriously staple papers on our desk.
我们真的会在办公桌上用它订纸。

1279
01:01:42.060 --> 01:01:45.520
So, do you think Steve was just, like, playing with the stapler he thought was cool?
所以，你觉得史蒂夫当时只是觉得那个订书机很酷才玩它的吗？

1280
01:01:46.020 --> 01:01:50.500
Because I don't know how to explain this air pressure mechanism of the stapler.
因为我不知道该怎么解释这个订书机的气压机制。

1281
01:01:50.500 --> 01:01:53.640
Okay, next time I'm over at your house, will you just show me the stapler?
好吧，下次我去你家的时候，你能给我展示一下那个订书机吗？

1282
01:01:53.780 --> 01:01:56.160
I seriously should have brought it in, because you can hear it.
我真该把它带过来，因为你能听到它的声音。

1283
01:01:56.240 --> 01:01:57.180
It's like, ka-chunk.
听起来就像是，咔哒一声。

1284
01:01:57.680 --> 01:01:58.000
Wow.
哇。

1285
01:01:58.180 --> 01:02:01.940
It's like having all the power of an industrial stapler.
就像拥有了工业级订书机的所有威力。

1286
01:02:02.220 --> 01:02:03.760
In the palm of your hand.
就在你的手掌之中。

1287
01:02:03.880 --> 01:02:05.460
You should do commercials for them.
你应该为它们拍广告。

1288
01:02:05.640 --> 01:02:06.440
I really should.
我真的应该拍。

1289
01:02:06.540 --> 01:02:07.800
They should sponsor us.
它们应该赞助我们。

1290
01:02:07.980 --> 01:02:09.560
It's just the push of your finger.
只要手指轻轻一按。

1291
01:02:09.700 --> 01:02:15.800
And when you do it, it's such an engineering marvel that you just want to staple everything
当你使用它时，那简直是一个工程奇迹，让你想把视线范围内

1292
01:02:15.800 --> 01:02:16.360
in sight.
的一切都订起来。

1293
01:02:16.500 --> 01:02:17.160
Well, good Lord.
天哪。

1294
01:02:17.240 --> 01:02:19.000
I need to see the stapler.
我一定要见识一下那个订书机。

1295
01:02:19.420 --> 01:02:22.300
Maybe I should do a video of myself stapling things.
也许我应该拍个视频，展示我订东西的过程。

1296
01:02:22.320 --> 01:02:22.560
Would you please?
你能拍吗？

1297
01:02:22.560 --> 01:02:25.140
And you can put it in the office of these Instagram stories.
你可以把它发到办公室的 Instagram 快拍里。

1298
01:02:25.160 --> 01:02:25.880
Give it to me.
给我看看。

1299
01:02:26.040 --> 01:02:27.040
We all need to see it.
我们大家都想看。

1300
01:02:27.100 --> 01:02:28.140
Okay, I'll do it.
好吧，我会拍的。

1301
01:02:28.280 --> 01:02:29.620
I need to hold it in my hand.
我得把它拿在手里。

1302
01:02:29.620 --> 01:02:30.500
I need to touch it.
我得摸摸它。

1303
01:02:30.640 --> 01:02:31.180
Wait a second.
等一下。

1304
01:02:31.320 --> 01:02:31.620
Wait a second.
等一下。

1305
01:02:31.620 --> 01:02:33.840
That is what she said.
她也是这么说的。

1306
01:02:34.280 --> 01:02:37.040
The minute I started going down that road, I was like, no, back up.
我刚开始往那个方向想，就觉得，不行，打住。

1307
01:02:37.040 --> 01:02:37.940
Wow.
哇。

1308
01:02:38.620 --> 01:02:40.020
Moving us along.
我们继续吧。

1309
01:02:40.240 --> 01:02:45.680
Lady, it is time to kick off this pancake luncheon.
女士，是时候开始这场煎饼午宴了。

1310
01:02:46.140 --> 01:02:47.400
Michael is outside.
迈克尔在外面。

1311
01:02:47.400 --> 01:02:50.880
He is making square pancakes for nobody yet.
他正在给还没到场的人做方形煎饼。

1312
01:02:51.160 --> 01:02:52.300
Ryan is texting.
瑞安在发短信。

1313
01:02:52.480 --> 01:02:54.840
I love that Michael's like, stop with the texting machine.
我喜欢迈克尔那种“别再玩那个发短信的机器了”的态度。

1314
01:02:54.840 --> 01:02:55.600
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1315
01:02:57.420 --> 01:03:02.780
So here we are, Jenna, at our second pair of sunglasses at 14 minutes, 59 seconds.
所以我们现在到了，珍娜，在14分59秒的时候，我们戴上了第二副太阳镜。

1316
01:03:03.040 --> 01:03:03.600
Oh, yes.
噢，没错。

1317
01:03:03.740 --> 01:03:05.280
I have the same time code.
我的时间码也是一样的。

1318
01:03:05.620 --> 01:03:08.040
What do you want to say about these sunglasses?
关于这副太阳镜你想说什么？

1319
01:03:08.460 --> 01:03:10.220
Wait, can we say it right at the same time?
等等，我们能同时说出来吗？

1320
01:03:10.380 --> 01:03:12.600
It'll be jarbled, but let's see if it sounds the same.
虽然会听不清，但看看听起来是不是一样。

1321
01:03:12.700 --> 01:03:12.980
Okay.
好。

1322
01:03:12.980 --> 01:03:23.120
These sunglasses were inspired by Joaquin Phoenix's appearance on The David Letterman Show in 2009
这副太阳镜的灵感来源于杰昆·菲尼克斯2009年在大卫·莱特曼秀上的亮相，

1323
01:03:23.120 --> 01:03:25.420
when he was promoting I'm Still Here.
当时他正在宣传《我仍在这里》。

1324
01:03:25.880 --> 01:03:27.340
It was a very odd appearance.
那次亮相非常古怪。

1325
01:03:27.340 --> 01:03:32.760
I watched that in real time, but it was all part of like a marketing ploy or something.
我当时实时看了直播，但这其实是某种营销策略之类的东西。

1326
01:03:32.960 --> 01:03:40.680
He did this film, and I guess he was trying to make us believe that he had actually switched
他拍了那部电影，我想他是想让我们相信他真的转行了，

1327
01:03:40.680 --> 01:03:45.040
careers, and it was sort of like an Andy Kaufman-esque thing.
这有点像安迪·考夫曼式的表演。

1328
01:03:45.500 --> 01:03:46.740
I took a screen grab.
我截了图。

1329
01:03:47.040 --> 01:03:50.360
I did a side-by-side for you, lady.
我为你做了一张对比图，女士。

1330
01:03:50.660 --> 01:03:51.920
Oh, give it to me.
噢，快给我看看。

1331
01:03:52.060 --> 01:03:55.200
Joaquin Phoenix and Ryan, same sunglasses.
杰昆·菲尼克斯和瑞安，戴着一样的太阳镜。

1332
01:03:55.660 --> 01:03:56.720
Putting that in stories.
发到快拍里。

1333
01:03:56.980 --> 01:03:58.980
They retail for about $400.
它们零售价大约400美元。

1334
01:03:59.580 --> 01:03:59.940
What?
什么？

1335
01:04:00.200 --> 01:04:01.240
For sunglasses?
买太阳镜？

1336
01:04:01.700 --> 01:04:01.920
Yeah.
是啊。

1337
01:04:02.520 --> 01:04:03.260
Are you crazy?
你疯了吗？

1338
01:04:03.400 --> 01:04:04.140
Are they prescription?
它们是近视镜吗？

1339
01:04:04.560 --> 01:04:05.980
No, they're just fancy.
不，它们只是时髦而已。

1340
01:04:06.120 --> 01:04:06.740
That's nuts.
太疯狂了。

1341
01:04:06.740 --> 01:04:12.340
I mean, if I bought that pair of sunglasses, I might as well just flush $400 down the toilet
我是说，如果我买了那副太阳镜，我还不如直接把400美元冲进马桶，

1342
01:04:12.340 --> 01:04:14.120
because I'm going to lose them in less than a year.
因为我不到一年就会把它们弄丢。

1343
01:04:14.340 --> 01:04:18.940
I know some people like fancy sunglasses, and listen, you do you, but I don't know.
我知道有些人喜欢时髦的太阳镜，听着，你开心就好，但我不知道。

1344
01:04:19.120 --> 01:04:22.920
Three kids, sunglasses, soccer games, mine just get wrecked.
三个孩子，太阳镜，足球比赛，我的眼镜只会弄坏。

1345
01:04:23.300 --> 01:04:28.300
I splurged on a pair of $200 prescription sunglasses.
我曾挥霍买过一副200美元的近视太阳镜。

1346
01:04:28.300 --> 01:04:30.120
I have to have prescription sunglasses.
我必须得戴近视太阳镜。

1347
01:04:30.120 --> 01:04:34.600
Because I was doing the double glasses for so long, you know, where you buy a giant pair
因为我戴双层眼镜戴了太久了，你知道的，就是买一副巨大的普通太阳镜，

1348
01:04:34.600 --> 01:04:37.960
of regular sunglasses that you put over your real glasses.
戴在你的真眼镜外面。

1349
01:04:38.220 --> 01:04:38.680
I saw it, Jenna.
我看到了，珍娜。

1350
01:04:38.780 --> 01:04:41.540
You look like you need to live in like a Florida retirement community.
你看上去就像需要住在佛罗里达的退休社区里一样。

1351
01:04:41.980 --> 01:04:42.120
I know.
我知道。

1352
01:04:42.260 --> 01:04:43.200
And you know what?
你知道吗？

1353
01:04:43.340 --> 01:04:48.040
I managed to keep those prescription sunglasses for almost two years.
我设法把那副处方太阳镜戴了快两年。

1354
01:04:49.040 --> 01:04:53.080
I lost them somewhere, and now I'm back to double glasses.
但我把它弄丢了，现在又得戴两副眼镜了。

1355
01:04:53.700 --> 01:04:55.000
You know what we need?
你知道我们需要什么吗？

1356
01:04:55.180 --> 01:04:55.460
What?
什么？

1357
01:04:55.760 --> 01:04:58.440
Josh says I need the chain on my glasses.
乔什说我需要给眼镜配条挂绳。

1358
01:04:59.060 --> 01:05:00.780
Oh, I have a story about my mom.
噢，我有个关于我妈的故事。

1359
01:05:00.940 --> 01:05:01.640
What happens?
怎么了？

1360
01:05:01.740 --> 01:05:02.440
That's it, right?
就是这样，对吧？

1361
01:05:02.540 --> 01:05:03.000
That's it.
就是这样。

1362
01:05:03.080 --> 01:05:04.300
Your sexy days are over.
你的性感日子到头了。

1363
01:05:04.460 --> 01:05:06.520
If you put your glasses on a chain, I don't know.
如果你给眼镜配了挂绳，我不知道会怎样。

1364
01:05:06.660 --> 01:05:12.520
Well, my mom, we affectionately call her Lucy because when you go into a store with her,
嗯，我妈，我们亲切地叫她露西，因为当你和她一起去商店时，

1365
01:05:12.740 --> 01:05:18.400
it's like you're shopping with Lucille Ball from I Love Lucy because she will manage to
就像和《我爱露西》里的露西尔·鲍尔一起购物一样，因为她总能

1366
01:05:18.400 --> 01:05:22.580
get tangled in or knock over any store display.
被商店的陈列架缠住或者把它们撞倒。

1367
01:05:22.780 --> 01:05:26.480
I was going to say, does she knock things over or try to put too many chocolates in her mouth?
我正想说，她是会撞倒东西，还是会试图往嘴里塞太多巧克力？

1368
01:05:26.480 --> 01:05:33.500
Well, so we were shopping with her, and she had on her glasses around one of those chains,
嗯，当时我们正陪她购物，她戴着那种挂绳眼镜，

1369
01:05:34.060 --> 01:05:39.860
but it was winter, so she also had a scarf, and she also had, I don't know why, like long
但那是冬天，所以她还围着围巾，而且我也不知道为什么，她还戴着长项链，

1370
01:05:39.860 --> 01:05:43.060
necklaces, a purse, you know, cross-bodied.
背着个斜挎包。

1371
01:05:43.520 --> 01:05:47.640
She goes to take off her cross-body purse.
她去摘斜挎包的时候，

1372
01:05:47.900 --> 01:05:50.500
It yanks on her sunglasses chain.
包带扯到了她的眼镜挂绳。

1373
01:05:50.800 --> 01:05:52.080
Elbows are flying.
手肘乱挥。

1374
01:05:52.300 --> 01:05:55.060
She takes down a whole display of earrings.
她撞倒了一整排耳环陈列架。

1375
01:05:55.460 --> 01:05:55.920
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1376
01:05:55.920 --> 01:06:00.560
My sister and I are, like, rushing in to, like, help her.
我和我姐赶紧冲过去帮她。

1377
01:06:00.660 --> 01:06:01.460
She's tangled.
她被缠住了。

1378
01:06:01.700 --> 01:06:07.280
She looks like a cat tangled in string, and just displays are falling down.
她看起来就像一只被毛线缠住的猫，陈列架全倒了。

1379
01:06:07.780 --> 01:06:14.300
So whenever I think about putting my glasses on a chain, that memory comes back to me,
所以每当我想给眼镜配挂绳时，那段记忆就会浮现，

1380
01:06:14.320 --> 01:06:16.060
and I think, that could be me.
我就想，那可能会是我。

1381
01:06:16.380 --> 01:06:17.580
I could be that.
我可能会变成那样。

1382
01:06:17.700 --> 01:06:19.280
I could easily have done that.
我完全可能做出那种事。

1383
01:06:19.580 --> 01:06:20.740
I could take down a display.
我可能会撞倒陈列架。

1384
01:06:21.220 --> 01:06:22.560
You could take down a display.
你确实可能会撞倒陈列架。

1385
01:06:22.840 --> 01:06:26.320
I saw you almost take out a few people on an airplane with a guitar.
我见过你在飞机上背着吉他差点撞到好几个人。

1386
01:06:26.860 --> 01:06:27.200
Yeah.
是啊。

1387
01:06:27.560 --> 01:06:27.820
Yeah.
是啊。

1388
01:06:28.300 --> 01:06:32.520
I mean, so I can't, I can't chain my glasses, is the bottom line.
我的意思是，我不能给眼镜配挂绳，结论就是这样。

1389
01:06:32.580 --> 01:06:33.060
Oh, well.
好吧。

1390
01:06:33.600 --> 01:06:34.300
I'm sorry.
我很遗憾。

1391
01:06:34.540 --> 01:06:34.800
Okay.
好吧。

1392
01:06:34.980 --> 01:06:42.860
But we spent $400 on these glasses for the character of Ryan for this very subtle inside
但我们花了400美元给瑞安这个角色配了这副眼镜，就为了一个非常隐晦的梗，

1393
01:06:42.860 --> 01:06:47.040
joke that clearly Ryan is a Joaquin Phoenix fan and probably saw that.
显然瑞安是华金·菲尼克斯的粉丝，可能看过那部电影。

1394
01:06:47.280 --> 01:06:48.160
It's in character.
这很符合角色设定。

1395
01:06:48.160 --> 01:06:51.700
He is the kind of guy who has to have the thing, the latest thing.
他就是那种必须拥有最新潮东西的人。

1396
01:06:52.140 --> 01:06:54.840
Even though his mom is driving him to work.
尽管他妈妈还在开车送他去上班。

1397
01:06:55.040 --> 01:06:55.420
Yes.
没错。

1398
01:06:55.700 --> 01:06:56.120
Exactly.
就是这样。

1399
01:06:56.540 --> 01:06:57.660
He's really not employed.
他其实没有工作。

1400
01:06:57.840 --> 01:06:59.080
Like, he's not earning a paycheck.
也就是说，他没有领薪水。

1401
01:06:59.240 --> 01:06:59.680
He isn't.
他不是。

1402
01:06:59.700 --> 01:07:01.560
He's going to get $400 sunglasses.
他要去买一副400美元的太阳镜。

1403
01:07:01.880 --> 01:07:08.040
At 15 minutes, 10 seconds, right as Pam is walking up, there's a great shot of some
在15分10秒的时候，就在帕姆走过来的时候，有一个很棒的镜头，拍到了一些

1404
01:07:08.040 --> 01:07:09.460
fakie grocery bags.
假冒的杂货袋。

1405
01:07:09.780 --> 01:07:10.740
Ooh, fakie bags.
噢，假冒的袋子。

1406
01:07:10.800 --> 01:07:12.160
We got some fakie bags.
我们有一些假冒的袋子。

1407
01:07:12.160 --> 01:07:18.120
And Jenna, you shared on the commentary something that jogged my memory.
珍娜，你在评论音轨里分享的一件事勾起了我的回忆。

1408
01:07:18.640 --> 01:07:21.640
It took me back immediately to this day.
它立刻把我带回了那一天。

1409
01:07:21.980 --> 01:07:27.660
You shared while you were filming this parking lot scene, the paparazzi snuck onto our set.
你分享说，在拍摄这个停车场场景时，狗仔队溜进了我们的片场。

1410
01:07:27.960 --> 01:07:29.760
Oh my gosh, I remember that.
天哪，我记得那件事。

1411
01:07:29.760 --> 01:07:31.640
Yes, we had a guy.
是的，我们当时有个家伙。

1412
01:07:32.040 --> 01:07:33.900
So, guys, we weren't on a big lot.
所以，伙计们，我们当时不在一个大型片场。

1413
01:07:34.080 --> 01:07:34.960
We've shared that before.
我们之前分享过。

1414
01:07:35.460 --> 01:07:36.820
We didn't have security.
我们没有安保人员。

1415
01:07:36.820 --> 01:07:37.900
You just drove in.
你直接开车进去就行了。

1416
01:07:38.040 --> 01:07:38.440
You did.
确实如此。

1417
01:07:39.000 --> 01:07:41.660
And after this day, we got a security guard.
在那天之后，我们就雇了一名保安。

1418
01:07:41.780 --> 01:07:42.660
In a little hut.
在一个小岗亭里。

1419
01:07:42.900 --> 01:07:43.160
Yeah.
是啊。

1420
01:07:43.320 --> 01:07:43.500
Yeah.
是啊。

1421
01:07:43.800 --> 01:07:48.480
This paparazzi guy clearly staked us out, realized you could just drive right on the set,
这个狗仔显然是蹲守了我们，意识到可以直接开车进入片场，

1422
01:07:48.480 --> 01:07:54.600
came right on, and just started clicking pictures of the set, the parking lot, actors
就直接进来了，开始对着片场、停车场、还有从拖车里

1423
01:07:54.600 --> 01:07:55.720
coming out of their trailers.
出来的演员拍照。

1424
01:07:55.900 --> 01:07:57.800
They got one of Steve coming out of his trailer.
他们拍到了一张史蒂夫从拖车里出来的照片。

1425
01:07:57.980 --> 01:08:00.380
And it took us all a while to be like, oh, who's that guy?
我们所有人都花了一会儿才反应过来，噢，那个人是谁？

1426
01:08:00.520 --> 01:08:00.980
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1427
01:08:01.120 --> 01:08:01.420
Oh, wait, wait.
噢，等等，等等。

1428
01:08:01.520 --> 01:08:01.800
We don't.
我们不知道。

1429
01:08:01.900 --> 01:08:02.720
No one knows that guy.
没人认识那个人。

1430
01:08:02.960 --> 01:08:06.380
Did I mention in the commentary why we think this happened?
我在评论音轨里提到过我们为什么认为会发生这种事吗？

1431
01:08:06.740 --> 01:08:08.260
Finally, after five seasons?
终于，在五季之后？

1432
01:08:09.140 --> 01:08:09.440
No.
没有。

1433
01:08:10.740 --> 01:08:12.880
John had started dating Emily Blunt.
约翰开始和艾米莉·布朗特约会了。

1434
01:08:12.980 --> 01:08:13.580
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1435
01:08:14.300 --> 01:08:14.700
Yeah.
是啊。

1436
01:08:14.700 --> 01:08:19.120
Yeah, so that was sort of tabloidy interesting.
是啊，所以那在小报看来挺有意思的。

1437
01:08:19.480 --> 01:08:19.860
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1438
01:08:20.060 --> 01:08:25.120
Until now, none of us did anything of tabloid interest, basically.
在此之前，我们基本上没人做过什么有小报价值的事。

1439
01:08:25.540 --> 01:08:25.860
No, no.
没有，没有。

1440
01:08:26.040 --> 01:08:29.040
So I remember this because I was dating Lee at the time.
所以我记得这件事，因为我当时正在和李约会。

1441
01:08:29.200 --> 01:08:32.860
He and I were starting to get serious, and John started dating Emily.
我和他开始认真交往了，而约翰也开始和艾米莉约会。

1442
01:08:33.360 --> 01:08:35.140
And we became couple friends.
然后我们成了情侣朋友。

1443
01:08:35.340 --> 01:08:35.660
You did.
你们确实是。

1444
01:08:35.740 --> 01:08:37.340
You guys would, like, go and do things.
你们会一起出去做些事情。

1445
01:08:37.540 --> 01:08:37.920
We did.
我们确实会。

1446
01:08:37.920 --> 01:08:42.840
And the news finally broke that the two of them were dating one another.
然后他们俩正在约会的消息终于传开了。

1447
01:08:42.840 --> 01:08:45.640
And I think that's why the paparazzi showed up.
我觉得这就是狗仔队出现的原因。

1448
01:08:46.000 --> 01:08:46.920
Maybe so.
也许是吧。

1449
01:08:47.140 --> 01:08:47.500
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1450
01:08:47.840 --> 01:08:50.940
Because it was just sort of, what, five years in out of nowhere.
因为这就像是，什么情况，五年了突然冒出来。

1451
01:08:50.940 --> 01:08:52.560
Oh, this guy wants pictures.
哦，这家伙想要拍照。

1452
01:08:53.540 --> 01:08:54.580
Yes, exactly.
没错，正是如此。

1453
01:08:54.940 --> 01:09:00.300
The one other time we had paparazzi show up was when we were shooting on location for Jim
我们唯一一次遇到狗仔队是在我们外景拍摄吉姆

1454
01:09:00.300 --> 01:09:01.080
and Pam's wedding.
和帕姆婚礼的时候。

1455
01:09:01.360 --> 01:09:02.020
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

1456
01:09:02.120 --> 01:09:03.180
Well, that would have been a big.
嗯，那确实是一件大事。

1457
01:09:03.360 --> 01:09:04.960
That was like a big show event.
那就像是一场大型的节目活动。

1458
01:09:05.080 --> 01:09:05.320
Yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊。

1459
01:09:05.460 --> 01:09:06.220
Within the show.
在剧集里。

1460
01:09:06.220 --> 01:09:09.540
But for the most part, we didn't have any of that stuff.
但大部分时间，我们根本没遇到过那种事。

1461
01:09:09.680 --> 01:09:10.840
We didn't, thankfully.
谢天谢地，我们没有。

1462
01:09:11.080 --> 01:09:14.360
I'm glad that we were our, just our little, tucked away little studio.
我很高兴我们只是我们那个隐蔽的小摄影棚。

1463
01:09:14.700 --> 01:09:15.440
I agree.
我同意。

1464
01:09:16.080 --> 01:09:21.140
I do think at one point, the paparazzi got a shot of me leaving my trailer with, like,
我确实记得有一次，狗仔队拍到了我离开拖车，手里拿着，呃，

1465
01:09:21.260 --> 01:09:23.300
my empty lunch plate.
我吃空的午餐盘子。

1466
01:09:24.120 --> 01:09:25.920
And it is the moSt.
那真是绝了。

1467
01:09:26.100 --> 01:09:27.740
That made me, like, short laugh.
那让我，呃，忍不住笑了一下。

1468
01:09:28.580 --> 01:09:32.320
It is just, like, the most unflattering photo.
那照片简直，就是最难看的照片。

1469
01:09:32.760 --> 01:09:33.500
That is so perfect.
那太完美了。

1470
01:09:33.500 --> 01:09:35.260
Of a person who has finished their lunch.
一个刚吃完午饭的人的照片。

1471
01:09:35.800 --> 01:09:39.420
I, I, this was years later, you guys.
我，我，那是几年后的事了，伙计们。

1472
01:09:39.600 --> 01:09:40.740
Like, the show had ended.
就像是，剧集已经结束了。

1473
01:09:41.080 --> 01:09:42.760
And I was vacationing.
我在度假。

1474
01:09:43.400 --> 01:09:48.260
And I was at a beach that I guess Maria Sharapova was at.
我在一个海滩上，我想玛丽亚·莎拉波娃也在那儿。

1475
01:09:49.420 --> 01:09:52.720
And the paparazzi clearly showed up for her.
狗仔队显然是冲着她来的。

1476
01:09:52.880 --> 01:09:55.140
But I was, like, side dish.
但我就像是，配菜一样。

1477
01:09:55.500 --> 01:09:57.040
So they got the photos of her.
所以他们拍了她的照片。

1478
01:09:57.100 --> 01:09:58.600
And then they snapped a few of me.
然后顺便拍了几张我的。

1479
01:09:58.860 --> 01:10:00.900
And it ended up in a tabloid magazine.
结果登在了一本小报杂志上。

1480
01:10:01.240 --> 01:10:02.900
And I saw the picture of me.
我看到了我的照片。

1481
01:10:03.280 --> 01:10:06.760
And I was, like, how do I send them a thank you?
我当时就在想，我该怎么给他们寄封感谢信呢？

1482
01:10:07.420 --> 01:10:09.840
Was it a really good picture of you on vacation?
那是你度假时拍的一张很棒的照片吗？

1483
01:10:09.840 --> 01:10:11.000
In my bathing suit.
穿着泳装。

1484
01:10:11.000 --> 01:10:13.620
And I was, like, I, I should thank someone.
我当时想，我，我应该感谢某个人。

1485
01:10:14.460 --> 01:10:17.540
I would say that we could put these photos in our stories.
我会说我们可以把这些照片放进我们的故事里。

1486
01:10:17.560 --> 01:10:21.920
But it's going to be, like, me hunching out of my empty food plate.
但那会是，呃，我端着空餐盘驼着背的样子。

1487
01:10:22.080 --> 01:10:23.760
And you vacationing in Mexico.
而你是在墨西哥度假。

1488
01:10:24.200 --> 01:10:26.040
I had just, like, been working out.
我当时刚，呃，健完身。

1489
01:10:26.140 --> 01:10:27.540
And I just want to sell someone.
我只想告诉某人。

1490
01:10:27.720 --> 01:10:28.100
Thank you.
谢谢。

1491
01:10:28.180 --> 01:10:29.440
Thanks for getting that for me.
谢谢你帮我拍下那个。

1492
01:10:30.040 --> 01:10:33.360
Well, since we're on the subject, I will just give this one more anecdote.
好吧，既然说到这个话题，我再讲一个轶事。

1493
01:10:34.120 --> 01:10:39.020
I really, really did not get photographed by the paparazzi ever.
我真的，真的从来没被狗仔队拍过。

1494
01:10:39.220 --> 01:10:40.060
And I still don't.
到现在也没有。

1495
01:10:40.060 --> 01:10:43.540
In fact, one time, I got in a car accident.
事实上，有一次，我出了车祸。

1496
01:10:43.800 --> 01:10:49.600
I was rear-ended by the paparazzi who were chasing Christina Ricci.
我被正在追逐克里斯蒂娜·里奇的狗仔队追尾了。

1497
01:10:49.920 --> 01:10:51.640
And I had to get out of my car.
我不得不下车。

1498
01:10:51.860 --> 01:10:52.020
Yeah.
是啊。

1499
01:10:52.120 --> 01:10:54.120
And we had to exchange all of our information.
我们不得不交换了所有信息。

1500
01:10:54.620 --> 01:10:55.920
The guy never took my picture.
那家伙自始至终都没拍我的照片。

1501
01:10:56.360 --> 01:10:57.700
In the whole exchange.
在整个交流过程中。

1502
01:10:58.580 --> 01:11:03.160
And then another time, I was out to dinner with Andy Roddick and Brooklyn Decker.
还有一次，我和安迪·罗迪克还有布鲁克林·黛克一起出去吃饭。

1503
01:11:03.360 --> 01:11:04.300
No one took your picture.
没人拍你的照片。

1504
01:11:04.520 --> 01:11:05.900
They swarmed them.
他们围住了他们。

1505
01:11:06.000 --> 01:11:07.900
And then everyone was taking their picture.
然后每个人都在拍他们的照片。

1506
01:11:08.280 --> 01:11:10.040
Someone said, hey, can you hold my camera?
有人说，嘿，你能帮我拿一下相机吗？

1507
01:11:10.300 --> 01:11:10.900
And Lee and I were behind them.
李和我当时就在他们身后。

1508
01:11:11.700 --> 01:11:11.900
Yeah.
是啊。

1509
01:11:12.100 --> 01:11:16.220
They were almost like, could you get out of the way of the picture of the beautiful people,
他们简直就像是在说，你们能让开一点吗，别挡着拍这些大美女帅哥，

1510
01:11:16.280 --> 01:11:16.460
please?
拜托？

1511
01:11:16.560 --> 01:11:20.080
You're really, you two are messing up our shot of the glamour couple.
你们俩真的在破坏我们拍这对魅力情侣的照片。

1512
01:11:20.080 --> 01:11:21.600
That was truly our story.
那确实是我们的故事。

1513
01:11:21.600 --> 01:11:26.060
Even when I was in the proximity of people being photographed by the paparazzi.
即使当我身处被狗仔队拍照的人附近时。

1514
01:11:26.420 --> 01:11:27.200
This is so true.
这太真实了。

1515
01:11:27.200 --> 01:11:27.640
No one cared.
根本没人关心。

1516
01:11:27.820 --> 01:11:28.260
So true.
太真实了。

1517
01:11:28.420 --> 01:11:29.000
I'm grateful.
我很感激。

1518
01:11:29.300 --> 01:11:30.100
Yeah, me too.
是啊，我也是。

1519
01:11:30.900 --> 01:11:31.340
All right.
好吧。

1520
01:11:31.620 --> 01:11:32.420
Moving on.
继续。

1521
01:11:33.140 --> 01:11:36.240
Jim has completed his rundown, everybody.
吉姆已经完成了他的工作总结，各位。

1522
01:11:36.580 --> 01:11:37.560
Huge news.
大新闻。

1523
01:11:37.940 --> 01:11:39.480
He presents it to Charles.
