I'm pretty sure he did.
我挺确定他去过。

1683
01:18:17.780 --> 01:18:18.640
I'm pretty sure he did.
我挺确定他去过。

1684
01:18:18.760 --> 01:18:19.440
I'm going to say that sounds right.
我觉得这听起来没错。

1685
01:18:19.520 --> 01:18:19.760
Okay.
好的。

1686
01:18:20.200 --> 01:18:22.140
Well, Ed really does play the banjo.
嗯，埃德确实会弹班卓琴。

1687
01:18:22.360 --> 01:18:26.440
In fact, Ed started a bluegrass band in college called The Lonesome Trio.
事实上，埃德在大学时组建过一个叫“孤独三重奏”的蓝草乐队。

1688
01:18:27.000 --> 01:18:29.320
Ed can play banjo guitar and piano.
埃德会弹班卓琴、吉他和钢琴。

1689
01:18:29.760 --> 01:18:35.060
And these guys, they just practiced together at lunch on the day of the scene to get this right.
而这两个人，为了把这一幕演好，就在拍摄当天的午餐时间一起练习。

1690
01:18:35.780 --> 01:18:35.940
Yeah.
没错。

1691
01:18:36.100 --> 01:18:38.280
You know, when they were filming it, everything was going well.
你知道，拍摄的时候，一切都很顺利。

1692
01:18:38.520 --> 01:18:44.180
And then they got to the part where Rain had to sing Take Me Home Country Road in German.
然后他们演到了雷恩必须用德语唱《带我回家，乡村路》的那部分。

1693
01:18:44.580 --> 01:18:44.980
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1694
01:18:44.980 --> 01:18:51.340
And something about having to do it in German and keep the tune and play the guitar while Ed's playing.
要用德语唱还要保持音准，同时在埃德伴奏下弹吉他，这对他来说有点难。

1695
01:18:51.520 --> 01:18:53.540
He was struggling a little bit.
他当时有点吃力。

1696
01:18:53.900 --> 01:18:56.720
So Randy said they got him really big cue cards.
所以兰迪说他们给他准备了很大的提示卡。

1697
01:18:57.280 --> 01:19:00.460
And they wrote out the German part of the lyrics phonetically.
他们把德语歌词用拼音标注了出来。

1698
01:19:00.780 --> 01:19:03.680
They had hired a translator to translate the song.
他们还专门雇了一位翻译来翻译这首歌。

1699
01:19:03.800 --> 01:19:04.080
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

1700
01:19:04.140 --> 01:19:06.420
He's really singing the lyrics in German.
他确实是在用德语唱那些歌词。

1701
01:19:06.600 --> 01:19:06.780
Yeah.
没错。

1702
01:19:07.040 --> 01:19:12.400
They put these huge cue cards right behind Ellie's shoulder just off camera.
他们把那些巨大的提示卡放在艾莉肩膀后方，刚好在镜头之外。

1703
01:19:12.400 --> 01:19:18.700
And I want you to know, if you go to 17 minutes, 47 seconds, Rain, right in that moment, I see you look at the cue card.
我想让你知道，如果你看到17分47秒，Rain，就在那一刻，我看到你在看提示卡。

1704
01:19:18.900 --> 01:19:19.760
You see him check it?
你看到他偷看了吗？

1705
01:19:19.860 --> 01:19:20.040
Yeah.
看到了。

1706
01:19:20.840 --> 01:19:22.260
I mean, that is hard.
我是说，那真的很难。

1707
01:19:22.440 --> 01:19:25.340
It's hard to sing a song you know in another language.
用另一种语言唱一首你熟悉的歌很难。

1708
01:19:25.980 --> 01:19:29.400
But also, it's a song you just learned on the guitar.
而且这还是你刚在吉他上学会的歌。

1709
01:19:29.580 --> 01:19:29.760
Yeah.
没错。

1710
01:19:29.960 --> 01:19:32.620
I remember one Christmas song I learned in Indonesian.
我记得我学过一首印尼语的圣诞歌。

1711
01:19:41.580 --> 01:19:43.860
We wish you a Merry Christmas.
祝你圣诞快乐。

1712
01:19:44.280 --> 01:19:44.820
Nice!
不错！

1713
01:19:45.340 --> 01:19:47.100
You guys know I grew up in Jakarta.
你们知道我是在雅加达长大的。

1714
01:19:47.300 --> 01:19:53.660
But there were times when you would learn a very sort of westernized song in a different language.
但有时你会用另一种语言去学一首非常西化的歌曲。

1715
01:19:54.220 --> 01:20:03.160
Well, did you notice that when Rain is singing in English, he actually gets the lyrics a little wrong?
对了，你们有没有注意到Rain唱英文歌词时，其实唱错了一点？

1716
01:20:03.500 --> 01:20:03.620
Yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊。

1717
01:20:03.680 --> 01:20:04.360
He flipped it.
他唱反了。

1718
01:20:04.480 --> 01:20:05.020
He did.
确实。

1719
01:20:05.280 --> 01:20:08.480
So the real lyrics are, country roads, take me home.
真正的歌词是“乡村路，带我回家”。

1720
01:20:09.240 --> 01:20:12.660
But Rain sings, take me home, country roads.
但Rain唱的是“带我回家，乡村路”。

1721
01:20:12.820 --> 01:20:13.020
Right.
没错。

1722
01:20:13.480 --> 01:20:15.400
Well, I just thought we had to hear this.
好吧，我只是觉得我们必须听听这个。

1723
01:20:15.640 --> 01:20:19.540
Can we hear Ed playing the banjo and Rain playing the guitar?
我们能听听艾德弹班卓琴，Rain弹吉他吗？

1724
01:20:20.200 --> 01:20:25.860
Take me home, country roads, to the place.
带我回家，乡村路，去那个地方。

1725
01:20:33.460 --> 01:20:36.580
Take me home, country roads.
带我回家，乡村路。

1726
01:20:48.460 --> 01:20:49.640
You have to stop.
你得停下来。

1727
01:20:50.840 --> 01:20:52.800
How fun is it to hear those guys play?
听他们俩演奏多有意思啊？

1728
01:20:53.040 --> 01:20:55.900
Well, I know they must have had so much fun doing that.
我知道他们当时一定玩得很开心。

1729
01:20:56.080 --> 01:21:00.620
I loved listening to it because it made me just think of them in real life.
我喜欢听这段，因为它让我联想到了现实生活中的他们。

1730
01:21:01.200 --> 01:21:01.680
Yeah.
是啊。

1731
01:21:02.020 --> 01:21:06.380
The only thing missing for me was Creed because, you know, Creed would have just been jamming on his mandolin.
对我来说唯一缺的就是克里德，因为你知道，克里德肯定会用他的曼陀林即兴演奏。

1732
01:21:06.720 --> 01:21:08.060
I just loved that moment.
我真的很喜欢那一刻。

1733
01:21:08.160 --> 01:21:12.740
One of the things I also loved was Justin said that, you know,
我喜欢的另一件事是贾斯汀说的，你知道，

1734
01:21:12.940 --> 01:21:20.000
this really showed the bromance because while the beginning they're trying to one-up each other and they're playing and they're playing over each other,
这真的展现了他们的兄弟情，因为虽然一开始他们试图胜过对方，互相较劲，演奏时盖过对方，

1735
01:21:20.160 --> 01:21:24.580
it ends up in just a bromance, mutual admiration club.
但最后变成了一种兄弟情，一个互相欣赏的俱乐部。

1736
01:21:24.760 --> 01:21:25.640
And Erin's not even there.
而且艾琳甚至都不在那里。

1737
01:21:25.800 --> 01:21:32.400
She walks away and now they're just looking at each other, harmonizing and jamming out and they're back.
她走开了，现在他们只是看着对方，和声并即兴演奏，然后又回到了状态。

1738
01:21:32.400 --> 01:21:41.680
Well, while I was researching this episode, I found this really cool quote from Ed where he talked about Andy's banjo playing on the show.
嗯，我在研究这一集时，发现了艾德关于安迪在剧中弹班卓琴的一段很酷的引语。

1739
01:21:41.840 --> 01:21:44.020
It's from an e-magazine article.
来自一份电子杂志的文章。

1740
01:21:44.020 --> 01:21:45.580
And here's what he said.
他是这么说的。

1741
01:21:45.780 --> 01:21:46.540
He said,
他说，

1742
01:21:46.740 --> 01:21:53.820
I'm happy to play my banjo at any opportunity I can get, but there's no real explanation why Andy plays the banjo.
只要有机会我都很乐意弹我的班卓琴，但安迪为什么会弹班卓琴并没有真正的解释。

1743
01:21:54.040 --> 01:21:57.660
It's so fun and weird, but he's a Connecticut preppy guy.
这很有趣也很奇怪，但他是个康涅狄格州的预科生。

1744
01:21:57.820 --> 01:21:59.240
How did he pick up a banjo?
他是怎么学会弹班卓琴的？

1745
01:21:59.500 --> 01:22:03.880
It's one of Andy's many mysteries, not all of which I even understand.
这是安迪的众多谜团之一，连我都没完全搞懂。

1746
01:22:04.960 --> 01:22:09.600
But I love that Andy plays the banjo, but Ed is so right.
但我喜欢安迪弹班卓琴的设定，不过艾德说得太对了。

1747
01:22:09.840 --> 01:22:14.320
Like, I never thought, how or why does Andy know how to play the banjo?
就像我从来没想过，安迪是怎么学会弹班卓琴的，或者为什么会弹？

1748
01:22:14.420 --> 01:22:15.860
Yeah, it doesn't clock at all.
是啊，这完全说不通。

1749
01:22:15.900 --> 01:22:19.020
And also that he could just pick up a sitar and play it, you know?
还有他竟然能随手拿起一把西塔琴就弹，你懂吗？

1750
01:22:19.020 --> 01:22:20.880
It's like he's so musically talented.
他好像非常有音乐天赋。

1751
01:22:21.140 --> 01:22:24.760
I get the acapella side, but this banjo is so specific.
我理解阿卡贝拉那部分，但这个班卓琴太特别了。

1752
01:22:24.960 --> 01:22:25.380
It is.
确实如此。

1753
01:22:25.900 --> 01:22:30.640
Well, sad to say, the pancake brunch was a little bit of a wash.
唉，遗憾的是，煎饼早午餐搞砸了。

1754
01:22:30.840 --> 01:22:31.220
Yeah.
是啊。

1755
01:22:31.220 --> 01:22:33.880
Other than the one dude, I don't think anyone came.
除了那一个人，我觉得根本没人来。

1756
01:22:34.040 --> 01:22:35.260
Creed and Meredith, that's it.
就克里德和梅雷迪思，没了。

1757
01:22:35.420 --> 01:22:35.640
Yeah.
是啊。

1758
01:22:36.140 --> 01:22:40.380
At 18 minutes, 22 seconds, we have a very sad shot of Michael.
在18分22秒处，有一个迈克尔看起来非常凄凉的镜头。

1759
01:22:40.640 --> 01:22:43.960
And the wind is blowing the paper all over.
风把纸吹得到处都是。

1760
01:22:44.860 --> 01:22:50.120
Randy told me that we set up huge special effects fans to create this wind.
兰迪告诉我，我们架设了大型特效风扇来制造这种风效。

1761
01:22:50.800 --> 01:22:59.080
That it would make the whole thing feel even sadder if all these papers were blowing around and the tablecloth was blowing in the wind.
说是如果这些纸到处乱飞，桌布也在风中飘动，会显得整个场景更加凄凉。

1762
01:22:59.080 --> 01:23:08.720
And then Gene told me that Randall, our cinematographer, spent almost an hour filming paper blowing across the parking lot.
然后吉恩告诉我，我们的摄影指导兰德尔花了将近一个小时拍摄纸张在停车场飘飞的画面。

1763
01:23:08.720 --> 01:23:11.660
Like, sad shots of paper blowing.
就是那种纸张飘飞的凄凉镜头。

1764
01:23:11.660 --> 01:23:12.080
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1765
01:23:12.080 --> 01:23:12.380
Blowing.
飘飞着。

1766
01:23:12.500 --> 01:23:14.340
He said we never used any of it.
他说我们最后根本没用上这些素材。

1767
01:23:14.380 --> 01:23:16.300
It's an hour of paper blowing footage.
那可是一个小时的纸张飘飞素材。

1768
01:23:16.460 --> 01:23:16.760
Yes.
没错。

1769
01:23:16.860 --> 01:23:20.520
That would have gone into the closet of tapes.
那些素材本该被塞进磁带储藏室里。

1770
01:23:20.900 --> 01:23:21.460
Somewhere.
某个角落里。

1771
01:23:22.000 --> 01:23:24.280
Which is now Michael Scott Paper Company.
也就是现在的迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司。

1772
01:23:24.840 --> 01:23:27.200
Well, now they're all really down in the dumps.
好吧，现在他们都非常沮丧。

1773
01:23:27.320 --> 01:23:29.780
They go back into their tiny closet office.
他们回到了那个狭小的壁橱办公室。

1774
01:23:29.780 --> 01:23:32.400
And you kind of feel like they're giving up.
你会觉得他们快要放弃了。

1775
01:23:32.620 --> 01:23:34.600
And then the phone rings.
然后电话响了。

1776
01:23:35.260 --> 01:23:36.900
And Pam answers it.
帕姆接了电话。

1777
01:23:37.820 --> 01:23:39.260
And guess what?
你猜怎么着？

1778
01:23:39.740 --> 01:23:41.060
It's Russell.
是拉塞尔。

1779
01:23:41.220 --> 01:23:42.040
The guy.
就是那个人。

1780
01:23:42.180 --> 01:23:42.840
From the paper luncheon.
那个参加煎饼午餐的人。

1781
01:23:43.000 --> 01:23:44.060
He wants paper.
他想要订纸。

1782
01:23:44.340 --> 01:23:45.020
He does.
他确实想要。

1783
01:23:45.400 --> 01:23:50.800
He places an order and Pam guarantees his satisfaction.
他下了订单，帕姆保证他会满意。

1784
01:23:50.800 --> 01:23:53.180
She guarantees it is her guarantee.
她保证，这是她的承诺。

1785
01:23:53.540 --> 01:23:53.840
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1786
01:23:54.500 --> 01:23:56.320
Pam has made her first sale.
帕姆完成了她的第一笔销售。

1787
01:23:57.280 --> 01:24:01.400
Not only the first sale of Michael Scott Paper Company, but her first sale.
这不仅是迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司的第一笔销售，也是她个人的第一笔销售。

1788
01:24:01.580 --> 01:24:03.940
They're going to tack a dollar up to the wall.
他们要把一美元贴在墙上。

1789
01:24:04.400 --> 01:24:05.820
It's a huge celebration.
这可是个大庆典。

1790
01:24:06.080 --> 01:24:07.760
Pam leaves with a spring in her step.
帕姆脚步轻快地离开了。

1791
01:24:07.920 --> 01:24:08.400
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

1792
01:24:08.600 --> 01:24:10.980
She runs out, gives Jim a kiss in the parking lot.
她跑出去，在停车场给了吉姆一个吻。

1793
01:24:11.080 --> 01:24:12.580
This is an amazing day.
这是极其美妙的一天。

1794
01:24:13.140 --> 01:24:15.460
Ryan's mom is there to pick him up.
瑞安的妈妈来接他了。

1795
01:24:15.740 --> 01:24:15.840
Sure.
当然。

1796
01:24:16.400 --> 01:24:19.260
Ryan's mom was played by Cindy Drummond.
瑞安的妈妈是由辛迪·德拉蒙德饰演的。

1797
01:24:19.260 --> 01:24:24.980
And there was actually a scene that got cut from the very top of the show of her dropping
其实在剧集开头还有一段被剪掉的戏，是她送

1798
01:24:24.980 --> 01:24:28.360
him off at work and giving him a sack lunch.
他来上班，还给了他一份午餐袋。

1799
01:24:29.060 --> 01:24:30.440
Cindy is an amazing actress.
辛迪是一位了不起的演员。

1800
01:24:30.620 --> 01:24:32.460
She's been in a ton of television comedy.
她出演过大量的电视喜剧。

1801
01:24:32.760 --> 01:24:34.840
Her scenes just got cut for time.
她的戏份只是因为时长原因被剪掉了。

1802
01:24:35.140 --> 01:24:38.900
It's really unfortunate because we were really lucky to have her on the show.
这真的很遗憾，因为能请到她来节目，我们真的很幸运。

1803
01:24:39.380 --> 01:24:40.760
I love that detail.
我很喜欢那个细节。

1804
01:24:40.980 --> 01:24:45.380
Every time I see her pull up in her station wagon, I just love it.
每次看到她开着旅行车过来，我都特别喜欢。

1805
01:24:45.380 --> 01:24:49.180
Well, the episode's going to end with Andy and Dwight.
嗯，这一集将以安迪和德怀特的场景结束。

1806
01:24:49.380 --> 01:24:51.080
They're just in such a great mood.
他们当时心情特别好。

1807
01:24:51.260 --> 01:24:52.500
They're walking through the kitchen.
他们正穿过厨房。

1808
01:24:53.040 --> 01:24:54.840
Oscar and Angela are sitting there.
奥斯卡和安吉拉坐在那里。

1809
01:24:55.140 --> 01:24:57.520
Angela does a massive eye roll.
安吉拉翻了一个大大的白眼。

1810
01:24:58.000 --> 01:25:01.460
And there was an Angela talking head that got deleted.
还有一个被删减的安吉拉的采访片段。

1811
01:25:02.260 --> 01:25:04.600
Dwight and Andy, friends.
德怀特和安迪，朋友。

1812
01:25:05.700 --> 01:25:09.480
I mean, what do those two possibly have in common?
我是说，这两个人到底有什么共同点？

1813
01:25:12.980 --> 01:25:14.560
She just takes a minute.
她停顿了一下。

1814
01:25:14.680 --> 01:25:16.980
And she's like, what could they possibly have in common?
然后她说，他们到底能有什么共同点呢？

1815
01:25:16.980 --> 01:25:20.240
And then looks at the camera like a little embarrassed.
接着有点尴尬地看向镜头。

1816
01:25:21.120 --> 01:25:23.660
That was Michael Scott Paper Company.
那是“迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司”那一集。

1817
01:25:24.920 --> 01:25:36.000
And next week is heavy competition, which happens to be Office Ladies 100th episode.
下周是“激烈竞争”，正好是《办公室女士》的第一百集。

1818
01:25:36.240 --> 01:25:37.660
I can't believe it.
我简直不敢相信。

1819
01:25:37.820 --> 01:25:38.120
Yeah.
是啊。

1820
01:25:38.500 --> 01:25:39.220
I can't believe it.
我简直不敢相信。

1821
01:25:39.340 --> 01:25:43.080
Driving into Earwolf today, I always call my mom on my drive.
今天开车去Earwolf的路上，我照例给我妈打了电话。

1822
01:25:43.220 --> 01:25:45.660
And she said, well, how many have you done?
她问我，你们做了多少集了？

1823
01:25:46.120 --> 01:25:47.800
She was like, are you almost done?
她问，你们快做完了吗？

1824
01:25:48.880 --> 01:25:51.380
I said, mom, we're coming up on 100.
我说，妈，我们快到一百集了。

1825
01:25:51.940 --> 01:25:53.300
She said, is that it?
她说，就这些吗？

1826
01:25:53.480 --> 01:25:54.980
I said, no, we're halfway.
我说，不，我们才做了一半。

1827
01:25:55.560 --> 01:25:56.320
Halfway there.
才完成了一半。

1828
01:25:57.560 --> 01:25:58.200
All right.
好吧。

1829
01:25:58.400 --> 01:26:04.020
So we will see you next week for Office Ladies 100th episode, heavy competition.
那么我们下周《办公室女士》第一百集“激烈竞争”再见。

1830
01:26:04.500 --> 01:26:06.060
